window.CATEGORIES=[{"id": "hype_lies", "label": "Hype machine / media & execs lying", "stakes": "S3", "scope": "political-economy", "count": 194, "instances": [{"date": "2024-02-19", "title": "Subprime Intelligence", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-fried", "quote": "Public companies are pumping their valuations and executive salaries off the back of artificial intelligence hype, yet nobody is saying the blatantly obvious — that this industry is deeply unprofitable and yet to prove its worth."}, {"date": "2024-02-19", "title": "Subprime Intelligence", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-fried", "quote": "And if this wasn't already worrying enough, one has to wonder what happens if we face another economic panic, or if the hype dies down before OpenAI or Anthropic discover a way to make a profit."}, {"date": "2024-03-18", "title": "Have We Reached Peak AI?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/peakai", "quote": "Yet his ultra-successful hype campaign was deeply specious, and he — along with the rest of the AI industry — has found himself suddenly having to deliver a future he's not even close to developing."}, {"date": "2024-03-18", "title": "Have We Reached Peak AI?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/peakai", "quote": "Artificial Hype Sam Altman desperately needs you to believe that generative AI will be essential, inevitable and intractable, because if you don't, you'll suddenly realize that trillions of dollars of market capitalization and revenue are being blown on something remarkably mediocre."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "If you believe the hype, selling AI infrastructure has helped Amazon Web Services — Amazon's cloud compute division — grow 12% year-over-year, Microsoft's Azure cloud services division increase revenue by 30% year-over-year, and Google's Cloud division grow revenue 28% year-over-year in its Q4 2023 earnings."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "For all this hype, I am seeing little evidence of actual adoption. While there are seemingly hundreds of different startups integrating AI on some level, it's unclear how deeply they integrate it, how essential it is to their operations, and whether it's actually making them any money."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "And when you cut through the hype, the AI industry is investing hundreds of billions of dollars to build infrastructure for a future that may never arrive based on the vague promise of hallucination-prone models."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "Perhaps it's because, despite the hype, there really isn't much to sell."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "Artificial intelligence isn't new, these models aren't new, and after just over a year of hype, generative AI is yet to prove it can do anything substantially different other than helping tech company CEOs raise money and create headlines."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "If businesses don't adopt AI at scale — not experimentally, but at the core of their operations — the revenue is simply not there to sustain the hype, and once the market turns, it will turn hard, demanding efficiency and cutbacks that will lead to tens of thousands of job cuts."}, {"date": "2024-04-15", "title": "They're Looting The Internet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-great-looting-of-the-internet", "quote": "What's so dangerous about AI for these companies is that despite all the hype, AI neither solves any real problems nor actually makes them any money."}, {"date": "2024-04-29", "title": "Managing Up", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/managing-up", "quote": "Yet because Altman — like every manager — is so thoroughly divorced from actual production, he’s only succeeded in generating unsustainable hype and making vague promises that the people who do the actual work at OpenAI likely know they can’t keep."}, {"date": "2024-05-13", "title": "Expectations Versus Reality", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/expectations-versus-reality", "quote": "The AI hype bubble, as I’ve noted before, is one entirely reliant on us accepting the idea of what these companies will do rather than interrogating their ability to actually do it."}, {"date": "2024-05-13", "title": "Expectations Versus Reality", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/expectations-versus-reality", "quote": "I’m not going to go through every single article that was written about the R1 before its announcement, but multiple outlets that are now crushing this device credulously accepted the “Large Action Model” as a done deal, which I would argue let ten thousand people buy this thing without really being given the truth."}, {"date": "2024-05-13", "title": "Expectations Versus Reality", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/expectations-versus-reality", "quote": "And when you really sit and think about it, the current AI hype cycle has done very little for society other than helping quasi-con-artists make millions of dollars."}, {"date": "2024-05-21", "title": "Sam Altman Is Full Of Shit", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-is-full-of-shit", "quote": "And unlike Sam Altman, both Sutskever and Leike are actual computer scientists that build things versus specious hype men who people have been trying to fire for a decade."}, {"date": "2024-05-21", "title": "Sam Altman Is Full Of Shit", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-is-full-of-shit", "quote": "He needs us to humor — even if he rejects the notion — the idea that AI could be considered a \"creature\" because doing so allows him to add further mystique and hype to distract from the fact that he doesn't seem to know anything and OpenAI doesn't seem to be innovating."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "He will push OpenAI to grow and sell into as many industries as possible, a specious hype-man selling to other specious hype-men desperate to connect their company to an AI bubble inflated by Altman himself."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "While ChatGPT isn’t inherently useless, Altman realizes that it’s impossible to generate the kind of funding and hype he needs based on its actual achievements, and that to continue to accumulate power and money, he must speciously hype it to wealthy and powerful people who don’t participate in the creation of anything."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "On some level, it’s kind of impressive how he’s succeeded in bending the tech industry to his whims, to the point that executives like Sundar Pichai of Google are willing to break their own products in pursuit of the next big hype-cycle."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "Altman may not actually create anything, but he’s excellent at spotting market opportunities — even if these opportunities involve him transparently lying about the technology he creates while having his boosters further propagate said lies either because they don’t know or don’t care that Altman is full of shit."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "All of this is thanks to Sam Altman and a tech industry that’s lost the ability to create things worthy of an actual hype cycle, to the point that a specious non-technical manipulator can lead it down a dark, ugly path."}, {"date": "2024-06-17", "title": "Let Tim Cook", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/untitled", "quote": "Apple treated ChatGPT with less excitement than a new suite of emojis, as an afterthought to a presentation that was deliberate in its lack of froth or hype."}, {"date": "2024-06-17", "title": "Let Tim Cook", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/untitled", "quote": "This year’s WWDC was framed as a series of fun, potentially even exciting features, all delivered with a continual promise of privacy and reliability that tacitly accepted that the AI hype train was moving too fast."}, {"date": "2024-06-17", "title": "Let Tim Cook", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/untitled", "quote": "And in this context, there’s no room for Altman — an unapologetic hype-man if there ever was one."}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "This report is so significant because Goldman Sachs, like any investment bank, does not care about anyone's feelings unless doing so is profitable. It will gladly hype anything if it thinks it'll make a buck."}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "Sequoia hype-man David Cahn gleefully mentioned in a recent blog that Nvidia's B100 will \"have 2.5x better performance for only 25% more cost,\" which doesn't mean a goddamn thing, because generative AI isn't going to gain sentience or intelligence and consciousness because it's able to run faster."}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "If there were some secret way that this would all get fixed, wouldn't Microsoft, or Meta, or Google, or Amazon — whose CEO of AWS compared the generative AI hype to the Dotcom bubble in February — have taken advantage of it?"}, {"date": "2024-07-16", "title": "Put Up Or Shut Up", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/put-up-or-shut-up", "quote": "There was nothing behind this, just like so much of the AI hype — a bunch of specious statements and empty promises in a wrapper of innovation despite creating nothing in the process."}, {"date": "2024-07-16", "title": "Put Up Or Shut Up", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/put-up-or-shut-up", "quote": "Generative AI's one real innovation is that it's allowed a certain class of scam artist to use the vague idea of \"powerful automation\" to hype companies to people that don't really know anything."}, {"date": "2024-07-24", "title": "Rot Economics - An Interview With MIT's Daron Acemoglu", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/rot-economics-an-interview-with-mits-daron-acemoglu", "quote": "You know, if you talk to business leaders today, everybody's asking them — financial journalists, their shareholders, and their friends — “where are you with the AI investment?” So that's the hype."}, {"date": "2024-07-24", "title": "Rot Economics - An Interview With MIT's Daron Acemoglu", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/rot-economics-an-interview-with-mits-daron-acemoglu", "quote": "And part of the reason why there is so much hunger for AI hype is that many people, including policymakers, are wishfully thinking “well, this could be a solution to our productivity slowdown."}, {"date": "2024-07-24", "title": "Rot Economics - An Interview With MIT's Daron Acemoglu", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/rot-economics-an-interview-with-mits-daron-acemoglu", "quote": "Also, on the AI field, I think the media is part of the reason why there is so much hype."}, {"date": "2024-07-29", "title": "How Does OpenAI Survive?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/to-serve-altman", "quote": "It means people are using it and not getting enough out of it, which could potentially lead to a significant loss of revenue as the hype cycle dies down."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "For reasons I’ve alluded to at the start of this article, investors are getting impatient with the AI hype boom — and, more specifically, with the giant tech companies that are bankrolling it."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "OpenAI began this hype cycle, Sam Altman is the PT Barnum of the Large Language Model circus, and it has absorbed more money and attention than any other startup of the last few years."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "To continue, Sundar Pichai of Google and Satya Nadella of Microsoft — as the loudest of the publicly-traded generative AI hype men — will have to show everybody something remarkable, but even then, they will have to show how it makes real money."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "This is the moment we find out if Sam Altman has really got it — whether it's worth wringing our hands about how scary he is, or whether he's just able to hoodwink enough credulous billionaires that have their hands welded to eternal money printers."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "And it’s all so craven. Big tech funded a cloud-dependent product that cost so much more than anything else on the market based on specious hype about what “artificial intelligence” can mean."}, {"date": "2024-08-12", "title": "Monopoly Money", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/monopoly-money", "quote": "Author: Ed Zitron Last week, in the midst of the slow, painful collapse of the generative AI hype cycle, something incredible happened."}, {"date": "2024-09-26", "title": "The Other Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/saaspocalypse-now", "quote": "This is why Marc Benioff is so excited to hype \"Agentforce,\" Salesforce's alleged \"autonomous AI agents\" that cost customers an incredible $2 a conversation."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "If OpenAI — which dominates with, I’d wager, at least a 30% market share — is only making $1 billion a year from selling access to its models, and at this stage in the massively-inflated hype bubble, there may not even be $10 billion of annual revenue from companies integrating generative AI into their products."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "OpenAI making so little selling access to their models suggests that, despite the hype-cycle, there either isn’t the interest in integrating these products from developers, or these integrations aren’t that useful, attractive or impressive to users."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "To continue growing ChatGPT Plus, it will have to create meaningful, mass-market use cases, or hope it can coast on a relatively-specious hype wave, one that will have to be so powerful it effectively triples its users."}, {"date": "2024-11-13", "title": "Lost In The Future", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/lost-in-the-future", "quote": "There is little moral quality to leaving X if your outlet continues to act as a stenographer for its leader, and this in fact suggests a lack of any real interest in change or progress, just the paper tiger of norms and values that will only end up depriving people of good journalism."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "While Anthropic's demo of its model allegedly controlling a few browser windows with a prompt might have seemed impressive to credulous people like Casey Newton, these were controlled demos which Anthropic added were \"slow\" and \"made lots of mistakes.\" Hey, almost like it's hallucinating!"}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "I feel sad and exhausted as I write this, drained as I look at the many times I’ve tried to warn people, frustrated at the many members of the media that failed to push back against the overpromises and outright lies of people like Sam Altman, and full of dread as I consider the economic ramifications of this industry collapsing."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "Altman, as discussed previously, is an artful bullshitter, having built a career out of being in the right places, having the right connections, and knowing exactly what to say — especially to a credulous tech media without the spine or inclination to push back on his more fanciful claims."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "If you ignore the hype, OpenAI and Anthropic are deeply boring software businesses with unprofitable, unreliable products prone to hallucinations, and their new products — such as OpenAI’s Sora — cost way too much money to both run and train to get results that, well, suck."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "It’s all been a con, a painfully-obvious one, one I’ve been screaming about since February 2024, trying to explain that beneath the hype was an industry that provided modest-at-best outcomes rather than resembling any kind of “next big thing.” Without “reasoning” as its magical new creation, OpenAI has nothing left."}, {"date": "2025-02-17", "title": "The Generative AI Con", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/longcon", "quote": "What These Oafs Are Actually Doing When you put aside the hype and anecdotes, generative AI has languished in the same place, even in my kindest estimations, for several months, though it's really been years."}, {"date": "2025-02-17", "title": "The Generative AI Con", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/longcon", "quote": "Despite the hype, the marketing, the tens of thousands of media articles, the trillions of dollars in market capitalization, none of this feels real, or at least real enough to sustain this miserable, specious bubble."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "On Unit Economics and Generative AI Putting aside the hype and bluster, OpenAI — as with all generative AI model developers — loses money on every single prompt and output."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "ChatGPT is sustained entirely on deranged, specious hype drummed up by a media industry that thinks it’s more remarkable to write down the last lie that Sam Altman told than say that OpenAI has lost $9 billion dollars in the last year and intends to more than double that number in 2025 for absolutely no reason."}, {"date": "2025-03-03", "title": "Power Cut", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/power-cut", "quote": "AI boosters will reply by saying there’s something I don’t know — that in fact Microsoft has some greater strategy, but answer me this: why is Microsoft canceling over a gigawatt of data center expansion?"}, {"date": "2025-03-03", "title": "Power Cut", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/power-cut", "quote": "But people are wondering, right now, why you didn’t write about this, and indeed why you seem more concerned with protecting the current market hype cycle than questioning it."}, {"date": "2025-03-17", "title": "CoreWeave Is A Time Bomb", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/core-incompetency", "quote": "While it’s hardly a recognizable name — like, say, OpenAI, or Microsoft, or Nvidia — this company is worth observing, if not for the fact that it’s arguably the first major IPO that we’ve seen from the current generative AI hype bubble, and undoubtedly the biggest."}, {"date": "2025-03-17", "title": "CoreWeave Is A Time Bomb", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/core-incompetency", "quote": "CoreWeave should have been a positive signal for generative AI, or at least a way for AI boosters to shut me up."}, {"date": "2025-03-24", "title": "The Phony Comforts of AI Optimism", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/optimistic-cowardice", "quote": "Newton is, along with his Hard Fork co-host Kevin Roose, actively engaged in a cynical marketing campaign, a repetition of the last two hype cycles where Casey Newton blindly hyped the metaverse and Roose pumped the bags of a penguin-themed NFT project."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "The Future of Generative AI Rests On OpenAI, And OpenAI's Future Rests On Near-Impossible Financial Requirements I have done my best to write this piece in as objective a tone as possible, regardless of my feelings about the generative AI bubble and its associated boosters."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "It's bullshit, but it captured the hearts and minds of AI boosters because it vaguely suggests that somehow Large Language Models and their associated technology will become something entirely different."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "OpenAI has the only meaningful userbase in generative AI, and this entire hype-cycle has been driven by its success, meaning any deterioration (or collapse) of OpenAI will tell the market what I've been saying for over a year: that generative AI is not the next hyper-growth market, and its underlying economics do not make sense."}, {"date": "2025-05-27", "title": "Desperate Times, Desperate Measures", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/measures", "quote": "We're three joyless years into this crap, and there isn't a single consumer product of note other than ChatGPT, a product that gained its momentum through a hype campaign driven by press and markets that barely understood what they were hyping."}, {"date": "2025-06-16", "title": "Sincerity Wins The War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sic", "quote": "Seriously, put aside the money, the hype, the pressure, the media campaigns, the emotions you have, everything, and just focus on the product as it is today. What is it that generative AI does, today, for you?"}, {"date": "2025-06-30", "title": "Make Fun Of Them", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/make-fun-of-them", "quote": "You don’t really have to be a specialist in anything to pry this shit apart, which is why so much of my work is either engaging to those who learn something from it or frustrating to those that intentionally deceive others through gobbledygook hype-schpiel."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "If you want to know my true agenda, it's that I see something in generative AI and its boosters something I truly dislike."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "As I wrote previously, Stargate doesn’t actually exist beyond the media hype it generated."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "The products don't do what they're meant to do, and people are realizing it. Nevertheless, boosters will still find a way to twist this study to mean something else."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Today, I’m going to give you the tools to fight back against the AI boosters in your life."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "I’m going to go into the generalities of the booster movement — the way they argue, the tropes they cling to, and the ways in which they use your own self-doubt against you."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "They’re your buddy, your boss, a man in a gingham shirt at Epic Steakhouse who won't leave you the fuck alone, a Redditor, a writer, a founder or a simple con artist — whoever the booster in your life is, I want you to have the words to fight them with."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "What Is An AI Booster?"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "AI Boosters Love Being Victims — Don’t Play Into It - BOOSTER QUIP: “You’re just being a hater for attention!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Contrarians just do it for clicks and headlines!” - AI Boosters Live In Vagueness — Make Them Get Specific - BOOSTER QUIP: “You Just Don’t Get It” - BOOSTER QUIP: “AI Is Powerful, and Getting Exponentially More Powerful” - Boosters Like To Gaslight — Don’t Let Them!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Boosters Do Not Live In Reality, So Force Them To Do So - BOOSTER QUIP: AI will- - BOOSTER QUIP: Agents will automate large parts- - BOOSTER QUIP: We're In The Early Days Of AI!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: Uhh, what I mean is that AI Is Like The Early Days Of The Internet!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: Well, actually, sir!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "The Early Days Of The Internet\" Are Not A Sensible Comparison To Generative AI - BOOSTER QUIP: Ahh, uh, what I mean is that we’re in the early days of AI!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: This Is Like The Dot Com Boom — Even If This All Collapses, The Overcapacity Will Be Practical For The Market Like The Fiber Boom Was!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: Umm, five really smart guys got together and wrote AI 2027, which is a very real-sounding extrapolation that- - ULTIMATE BOOSTER QUIP: The Cost Of Inference Is Coming Down!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "ULTIMATE BOOSTER QUIP: OpenAI and Anthropic are “just like Uber,” because Uber burned $25 billion over the course of 15 or so years, and is now profitable!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: Data centers are important economic growth vehicles, and are helping drive innovation and jobs throughout America!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: Uber burned a lot of money — $25 billion or more!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "ULTRA BOOSTER QUIP!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "AI Is Just Like Amazon Web Services — a massive investment that “took a while to go profitable” and “everybody hated Amazon for it” - [BOOSTER QUIP: \\[AI Company\\] Has $Xm Annualized Revenue!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "- BOOSTER QUIP: \\[AI Company\\] Is In “Growth Mode” and Will “Pull The Profit Lever When It’s Time” - BOOSTER QUIP: AGI Will- - BOOSTER QUIP: I’m Hearing From People Deep Within The AI Industry That There’s Some Sort Of Ultra Powerful Models They’re Not Talking About - BOOSTER QUIP: ChatGPT Is So Popular!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "ChatGPT (and OpenAI) Was Marketed Based On Lies - If I Was Wrong, We'd Have Real Use Cases By Now, And Better Metrics Than \"Weekly Active Users\" - BOOSTER QUIP: OpenAI is making tons of money!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: When OpenAI Opens Stargate Abilene, It’ll Turn Profitable?"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER (or well-meaning person) QUIP: Well my buddy’s friend’s dog’s brother uses it and loves it/Well I Heard This Happened, Well It’s Useful To Me."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "It Doesn't Matter That You Have One Use Case, That Doesn't Prove Anything - BOOSTER QUIP: Vibe Coding Is Changing The World, Allowing People Who Can’t Code To Make Software - I Am No Longer Accepting Half-Baked Arguments What Is An AI Booster?"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "So, an AI booster is not, in many cases, an actual fan of artificial intelligence."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "No, the AI booster is symbolically aligned with generative AI."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Kevin Roose and Casey Newton are two of the most notable boosters, and — as I’ll get into later in this piece — neither of them have a consistent or comprehensive knowledge of AI."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Thomas Ptacek’s “My AI Skeptic Friends Are All Nuts” was catnip for boosters, a software engineer using technical terms like “interact with Git” and “MCP,” vague charts, and, of course, an extremely vague statement that says hallucinations aren’t a problem: Is it?"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Anyway, my favourite part of the blog is this: Nobody projects more than an AI booster."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Also, none of the booster arguments actually survive a thorough response, as Nik Suresh proved with his hilarious and brutal takedown of Ptacek’s piece."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "I’m sorry if you are an AI booster and this makes you feel bad."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "allow these people to act as if they are being victimized or “othered.” BOOSTER QUIP: “You’re just being a hater for attention!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Contrarians just do it for clicks and headlines!” First and foremost: there are boosters at pretty much every major think tank, government agency and media outlet."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "It’s extremely lucrative being a booster."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Being a booster is the easy path! Being a critic requires you to constantly have to explain yourself in a way that boosters never have to."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "If a booster says this to you, ask them to explain: - What they mean by “clicks” or “attention,” and how they think you are monetizing it."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Boosters are more successful, get more perks and are in general better-treated than any critic."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "AI Boosters Live In Vagueness — Make Them Get Specific Fundamentally, these people exist in the land of the vague."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: “You Just Don’t Get It” Here’s a great place to start: say “that’s a really weird thing to say!” It is peculiar to suggest that somebody doesn’t get how to use a product, and that we, as the customer, must justify ourselves to our own purchases."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "If a booster suggests you “just don’t get it,” ask them to explain: - What you are missing."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: “AI Is Powerful, and Getting Exponentially More Powerful” If a booster refers to AI “being powerful” and getting “more powerful,” ask them: - What powerful means."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Boosters Like To Gaslight — Don’t Let Them!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "The core of the AI booster’s argument is to make you feel bad. They will suggest you are intentionally not liking A.I."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "So, here’s a really easy way to deal with this: if a booster ever suggests you are stupid or ignorant, ask them why it’s necessary to demean you to get their point across!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Even if you are unable to argue on a technical level, make them explain why the software itself can’t convince you. Boosters Do Not Live In Reality, So Force Them To Do So Boosters will do everything they can to pull you off course."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Print this and feed it to your local booster today."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: AI will- Anytime a booster says “AI will,” tell them to stop and explain what AI can do, and if they insist, ask them both when to expect the things they’re talking about, and if they say “very soon,” ask them to be more specific."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: Agents will automate large parts- There’s that “will” bullshit again."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Hell, in 2006 (the year before the iPhone launch), there was an estimated 17.7 million worldwide smartphone shipments (mostly from BlackBerry and other companies building on Windows Mobile, with Palm vacuuming up the crumbs), though to be generous to the generative AI boosters, I’ll disregard those."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: Ahh, uh, what I mean is that we’re in the early days of AI!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "AI 2027 was written specifically to fool people that wanted to be fooled, with big charts and the right technical terms used to lull the credulous into a wet dream and New York Times column where one of the writers folds their hands and looks worried."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "ULTIMATE BOOSTER QUIP: The Cost Of Inference Is Coming Down!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: \\[AI Company\\] Has $Xm Annualized Revenue! As I’ve discussed in the past, this metric is basically “monthx12,” and while it’s a fine measure for high-gross-margin businesses like SaaS companies, it isn’t for AI."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: AGI Will- There’s that “will” bullshit, once again, always about the “will.” We do not know how thinking works in humans and thus cannot extrapolate it to a machine, and at the very least human beings have the ability to re-evaluate things and learn, a thing that LLMs cannot do and will never do."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: I’m Hearing From People Deep Within The AI Industry That There’s Some Sort Of Ultra Powerful Models They’re Not Talking About This, too, is hogwash, nothing different than your buddy’s friend’s uncle who works at Nintendo that says Mario is coming to PlayStation."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Ask for specifics. BOOSTER QUIP: ChatGPT Is So Popular!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Every single time you hear \"AI\" you’re made to think of \"ChatGPT” by a tech media that has never stopped to think about their role in hype, or their responsibility to their readers."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "And as this hype has grown, the publicity compounds, because the natural thing for a journalist to do when everybody is talking about something is to talk about it more."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "I mean, again, what?” Credulousness aside, the GPT-4 marketing campaign was incredibly effective, creating an aura that allowed OpenAI to take advantage of the vagueness of its offering as people — including members of the media — willfully filled in the blanks for them."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: OpenAI is making tons of money!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: When OpenAI Opens Stargate Abilene, It’ll Turn Profitable? How?"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Stories and Booster Quips You May Have Heard That Are Bullshit Or Questionable - QUIP: \"Using AI Led Researchers To Discover 44% More Materials!\" - MIT has now withdrawn this paper citing concerns about its \"integrity.\" Here's a good rundown."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "that LLMs aren't incapable of this, they're insufficient. He claims they're also \"not dead weight for science,\" then spends hundreds of words meandering around to kiss up to AI boosters for some reason."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Vibe coding\" does not work, it will not work, and pretending otherwise is at best ignorance and at worst supporting a campaign built on lies. I Am No Longer Accepting Half-Baked Arguments If you are an AI booster, please come up with better arguments."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Then again, there are many well-intentioned people who aren't necessarily AI boosters who repeat these arguments, regardless of how thinly-framed they are, in part because we live in a high-information, low-processing society where people tend to put great faith in people who are confident in what they say and sound smart."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "By comparison, AI boosters are the first to get TV appearances and offers to be on panels, their coverage featured prominently on Techmeme, selling slop-like books called shit like The Future Of Intelligence: Masters Of The Brain featuring 18 interviews with different CEOs that all say the same thing."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "This newness and hype and these expectations sent the market into a frenzy, with every hyperscaler immediately creating the most aggressive market for one supplier I’ve ever seen."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "The thing is, Artificial Intelligence is built and sold on not just faith, but a series of myths that the AI boosters expect us to believe with the same certainty that we treat things like gravity, or the boiling point of water."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "To quote Merchant again, “\\[AI hype\\] has created the cover necessary to justify slashing rates and accepting “good enough” automation output for video games and media products.” Yet the jobs crisis facing translators speaks to the larger flaws of the Large Language Model era, and why other careers aren’t seeing this kind of disruption."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "Generative AI was always set up to fail, because it was meant to be everything, was talked about like it was everything, is still sold like it’s everything, yet for all the fucking hype, it all comes down to two companies: OpenAI, and, of course, NVIDIA."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "That alone is a very, very bad sign, especially as we’re three years and $500 billion or more into this hype cycle with few signs of life outside of, well, OpenAI promising people money."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "To look through the eyes of an AI booster — all I’m seeing is blue and yellow, as usual!"}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "I will make a good faith effort to explain every single failing, because my concern is the truth, and I would love everybody else to follow suit. Do you think any booster will have the same courtesy?"}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "I believe that they outnumber the boosters, the analysts and the hype-fiends that have propped up this era."}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "How To Argue With An AI Booster, a comprehensive guide to arguing with AI boosters, addressing both their bad faith debate style and their specific (and flimsy) arguments as to why generative AI is the future."}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "It's easy to feel isolated by the amount of hogs oinking at the prospect of laying you off or replacing you - and it turns out there are far more people that are afraid or outraged than there are executives or AI boosters."}, {"date": "2026-02-26", "title": "On NVIDIA and Analyslop", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/on-nvidia-and-analyslop", "quote": "Similarly, I make the effort to understand the underlying business models in a way that I’m not sure everybody else is trying to, and if I’m wrong, please show me an analysis of the financial condition of OpenAI or Anthropic from a booster."}, {"date": "2026-02-26", "title": "On NVIDIA and Analyslop", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/on-nvidia-and-analyslop", "quote": "As I said earlier, the “wow, Claude Code!” articles are mostly from captured boosters and people that do not actually build software being amazed that it can burp up its training data and make an impression of software engineering."}, {"date": "2026-03-03", "title": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-bubble-is-an-information-war", "quote": "Even Claude Code, the second coming of Christ in the minds of some of Silicon Valley’s most concussed boosters, only made $203m in revenue ($2.5bn ARR) for a product that at times involves Anthropic spending anywhere from $8 to $13.50 for every dollar it makes."}, {"date": "2026-03-10", "title": "The Beginning Of History", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-beginning-of-history", "quote": "And even in the very, very unlikely event that things somehow quickly return to whatever level of “normal” you’d call the world before the conflict started, even brief shocks to the financial plumbing are enough to destabilize an already-fractured hype cycle."}, {"date": "2026-03-10", "title": "The Beginning Of History", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-beginning-of-history", "quote": "The exact quote from the affidavit is that “...\\[Anthropic\\] has generated substantial revenue since entering the commercial market—exceeding $5 billion to date,” and while boosters will say “uhm, it says “exceeding,” if it were anything higher than $5.5 billion Anthropic would’ve absolutely said so."}, {"date": "2026-03-10", "title": "The Beginning Of History", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-beginning-of-history", "quote": "I do not see boosters doing the same to prove their points."}, {"date": "2026-03-10", "title": "The Beginning Of History", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-beginning-of-history", "quote": "It takes actual courage to form an opinion, something boosters fundamentally lack."}, {"date": "2026-03-10", "title": "The Beginning Of History", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-beginning-of-history", "quote": "The assumption boosters make is that one can fuck around forever."}, {"date": "2026-03-17", "title": "Why Are We Still Doing This?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/why-are-we-still-doing-this", "quote": "I know everybody is super excited about the supposed power of AI, but I think it’s time we set some fair ground rules going forward so we stop acting so crazy. Let’s start with a simple one: AI boosters are no longer allowed to explain what’s good about AI using the future tense."}, {"date": "2026-03-17", "title": "Why Are We Still Doing This?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/why-are-we-still-doing-this", "quote": "For an industry so thoroughly steeped in cold, hard rationality, AI boosters are so quick to jump to flights of fancy — to speak of the mythical “AGI” and the supposed moment when everything gets cheaper and also powerful enough to be reliable or effective. I hear all this crap about AI changing everything, but where’s the proof?"}, {"date": "2026-03-17", "title": "Why Are We Still Doing This?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/why-are-we-still-doing-this", "quote": "Even the boosters are beginning to worry."}, {"date": "2026-03-17", "title": "Why Are We Still Doing This?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/why-are-we-still-doing-this", "quote": "Where is the same effort from the AI boosters?"}, {"date": "2026-03-24", "title": "The AI Industry Is Lying To You", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-industry-is-lying-to-you", "quote": "The smug, condescending army of AI boosters exists to make you look away from the harsh truth — AI makes very little revenue, lacks tangible productivity benefits, and seems to, at scale, actively harm the productivity and efficacy of the workers that are being forced to use it."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "Boosters will again use this talking point to say that “we’re in the early days,” but that’s only true if you think that “early days” means “people aren’t really using it yet.” Yet the “early days” argument is inherently deceptive."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "While the Large Language Model hype cycle might have only begun in 2022, the entirety of the media and markets have focused their attention on AI, along with hundreds of billions of dollars of venture capital and nearly a trillion dollars of hyperscale capex investment."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "You paid $100 million, and then it made $200 million of revenue.” Yes, I know it’s a “stylized fact” or whatever, but that’s what he said, and I think that their IPO might have a rude surprise in the form of a non-EBITDA margin calculation that makes even the most-ardent booster see red."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "Anthropic’s $14 billion in annualized revenue from February 16, 2026 includes both the launch of Claude Opus 4.6, as well as the height of the OpenClaw hype cycle where people were burning hundreds of dollars of tokens a day."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "Because we’re still in the AI hype cycle, this kind of wasteful spending is both tolerated and encouraged, and the second that financial conditions worsen or stock prices drop due to increasing operating expenses, these same companies will cut back on API spend, which will overwhelmingly crush Anthropic’s glowing revenues."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "Even if you’re an AI booster, surely you want to know the truth, right?"}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "It’s even weirder considering that TBPN was already a booster for OpenAI!"}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "You’ll notice that most AI boosters have some sort of bizarre, overly-complicated way of explaining how they use AI."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "This is the core problem with the “checkmate, boosters — AI can write code!” problem."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "A Scenario Illustrating How Anthropic Fucks Over Its Customers It’s January 14 2026, and you just read The Atlantic’s breathless hype-slop about Claude Code, believing that it was “bigger than the ChatGPT moment,” that it was an “inflection point for AI progress,” and that it could build whatever software you imagined."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "Every one of those effusive, breathless hype-screeds about Claude Code from January or February 2026 are discussing a product that no longer exists."}, {"date": "2026-04-21", "title": "Four Horsemen of the AIpocalypse", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/four-horsemen-of-the-aipocalypse", "quote": "The endless, breathless support from the media runs cover for the deterioration of its services."}, {"date": "2026-04-21", "title": "Four Horsemen of the AIpocalypse", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/four-horsemen-of-the-aipocalypse", "quote": "Anthropic is a con, and said con is only made possible through endless, specious hype."}, {"date": "2026-04-21", "title": "Four Horsemen of the AIpocalypse", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/four-horsemen-of-the-aipocalypse", "quote": "Cal Newport has an excellent piece debunking the hype, but my general feeling is that if Mythos was so powerful, how did Claude Code’s source code leak?"}, {"date": "2026-04-21", "title": "Four Horsemen of the AIpocalypse", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/four-horsemen-of-the-aipocalypse", "quote": "Every new story that runs about cost-cutting or horrible burnrates increasingly validates my position, and for the most part, boosters respond by saying “well LOOK at how BIG the REVENUES are.” It isn’t!"}, {"date": "2026-04-21", "title": "Four Horsemen of the AIpocalypse", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/four-horsemen-of-the-aipocalypse", "quote": "In any case, I keep coming back to the word “hysteria,” because it’s hard to find another word to describe this hype cycle."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "And once everybody switches to token-based billing, I’m not sure we’ll see quite as much hype around generative AI."}, {"date": "2026-05-06", "title": "Am I Meant To Be Impressed?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/am-i-meant-to-be-impressed", "quote": "If that were the case, why does Anthropic need to raise one hundred and eight billion fucking dollars in less than three quarters? Time to make up some booster talking points and get mad at them: - Well actually Ed this is because Anthropic is taking advantage of the dumb money that wants to boost its valuation."}, {"date": "2026-05-06", "title": "Am I Meant To Be Impressed?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/am-i-meant-to-be-impressed", "quote": "Not a single one of my critics or any AI booster has put an iota of the same amount of effort into proving their case."}, {"date": "2026-05-19", "title": "AI Is Too Expensive", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-too-expensive", "quote": "Here’s a fun game: ask an AI booster how OpenAI or Anthropic becomes profitable!"}, {"date": "2026-05-19", "title": "AI Is Too Expensive", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-too-expensive", "quote": "One of you fucking AI boosters, answer me, how does this actual reverse course?"}, {"date": "2026-05-21", "title": "Anthropic's \"Profitability\" Swindle", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/anthropics-profitability-swindle", "quote": "I can imagine this has felt like a big victory for boosters — proof that AI can be profitable, that inference is profitable, that some sort of business model is emerging…and I’m sorry, that’s not what’s happening."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "The aggression with which AI boosters and executives act toward those who aren’t impressed suggests a genuine intellectual and moral weakness."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "This is why being an AI booster requires you to debase yourself."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Every AI booster will say “AI is writing all the code at some organizations,” but never seem to explain what happens as a result, such as whether software is being shipped faster, or better software is being made, or, well…anything. The answer is simple: they don’t know because nothing has actually changed."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "In truth, the amount of money that NVIDIA needs to keep this going is so extreme that it is now a test of how long the debt markets and the hyperscalers can keep sustaining the hype."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Nevertheless, even the sweatiest, least-trustworthy boosters have begun to sneak in statements about “we’re probably not in a bubble,“ or “yeah it’s a bubble, but it’s a good bubble.” Jeff Bezos, when asked about the AI bubble, said that you “shouldn’t worry about it,” which…is not really sufficient, is it Jeff?"}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "As a result, every frothy, fluffy hype-piece about Claude Code or AI in general is a kalopsia — the belief that something is more beautiful than it really is."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "Every frothy hype-piece you’ve read has been written by somebody who has been conned into ignoring the true cost of AI, all in service of spreading a technology that’s unreliable, inconsistent and expensive at its core, and never, ever seems to get cheaper."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "Four years and a trillion dollars in, AI is more expensive, its companies more cash-intensive, its products just as unreliable, and its boosters more desperate than ever to make you ignore reality as a means of empowering one of a few ultra-rich oafs."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "Every part of this bubble relies upon the momentum of hype to substantiate every link in the chain."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "This hype was unsustainable without buckets of lies, misinformation and a captured tech and business media."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "LLM Users Are The Victims Of A Con If AI had ROI, we’d be able to point with specificity to inarguable examples of economic impacts. AI boosters can jerk their binguses all they like about how Spotify’s CEO said its best engineers don’t write any code anymore."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "I’ve talked to a few people who describe LLMs normally, without hype, who tell very specific stories of very specific outcomes that save indeterminate amounts of time."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "When some of you are pushed to prove the ROI of AI, you immediately return to boring talking points about Uber, or the Dot Com Bubble, or some other slop fed to you by people actively conning you at this very moment. I mean this with as much empathy as I can muster: if you’re a huge AI booster, why do you defend this so vociferously?"}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "Last week I went on Bloomberg and discussed the state of the AI bubble with a clarity that rattled even the sweatiest boosters, mostly because I spoke with clarity about an investment frenzy whipped up through hype, deceit and mythology."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "This is a hysterical era perpetuated by liars, cowards, imbeciles, craven boosters and the easily-fooled."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "Boosters will say that it’s “hard to measure productivity for any job outside of sales,” but that’s simply not true!"}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "So many of you truly love making good software and want to do good things in the world and feel impeded by the Business Idiots and mocked by the boosters who seem to care more about your bosses than anything to do with software or innovation."}], "verdict": "Overstated, and worse over time", "analysis": "A real kernel overdrawn into his signature error. Executives do overpromise on imminent AGI and unattended agents, and much coverage was credulous. But by 2026 <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_hype_lies__c4\" data-tip=\"cat_hype_lies__c4\" href=\"https://uvik.net/blog/ai-coding-assistant-statistics/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the central hype, that this is a genuinely transformative technology, especially for coding, has been substantially vindicated</a>, unlike the crypto hype he equated it with. Calling nearly all of it lies was the mistake, and repeating it after the agentic shift is a failure to update. <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_hype_lies__c2\" data-tip=\"cat_hype_lies__c2\" href=\"https://techblog.comsoc.org/2025/10/04/amazons-jeff-bezos-at-italian-tech-week-ai-is-a-kind-of-industrial-bubble/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The same leaders he brands liars now openly concede bubble risk</a>, so <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_hype_lies__c3\" data-tip=\"cat_hype_lies__c3\" href=\"https://www.finance-monthly.com/sundar-pichai-ai-bubble-burst-warning/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">they are not simply lying either</a>.", "srcs": [["Altman warns AI market is in a bubble (CNBC, Aug 2025)", "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/08/18/openai-sam-altman-warns-ai-market-is-in-a-bubble.html"], ["Bezos: AI is an industrial bubble but society benefits (CNBC, Oct 2025)", "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/10/03/jeff-bezos-ai-in-an-industrial-bubble-but-society-to-benefit.html"], ["Pichai: no company immune if AI bubble bursts (Axios, Nov 2025)", "https://www.axios.com/2025/11/18/google-ceo-ai-bubble-warning-stock-market"]]}, {"id": "unprofitable", "label": "Unprofitable / can't survive / will collapse", "stakes": "S6", "scope": "company", "count": 172, "instances": [{"date": "2024-02-19", "title": "Subprime Intelligence", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-fried", "quote": "Public companies are pumping their valuations and executive salaries off the back of artificial intelligence hype, yet nobody is saying the blatantly obvious — that this industry is deeply unprofitable and yet to prove its worth."}, {"date": "2024-02-19", "title": "Subprime Intelligence", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-fried", "quote": "This situation is only made more problematic by the fact that these models are unprofitable, and Altman's desperation for a new chip company or energy breakthrough suggests that they'll only become more unprofitable as they generate more revenue."}, {"date": "2024-02-27", "title": "Software Has Eaten The Media", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-anti-economy", "quote": "In a logical tech economy, one would be terrified that so many bets have been made on such shaky ground, but we're in the Rot Economy, where an unsustainable product with few clear use cases can burn billions of dollars and fuel our climate crisis because the tech industry has run out of fucking ideas."}, {"date": "2024-03-11", "title": "Are We Watching The Internet Die?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/are-we-watching-the-internet-die", "quote": "Generative AI might be steeped in the language of high fantasy, but it’s a tool, one that they will not admit is a terribly-flawed and unprofitable way to feed the growth-at-all-costs tech engine."}, {"date": "2024-03-18", "title": "Have We Reached Peak AI?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/peakai", "quote": "If the AI bubble pops, the entire tech industry will suffer as venture capitalists are once again washed out through chasing an unprofitable, barely-substantiated trend."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "Running Sora is likely deeply unprofitable, and reducing its generative hallucinations — monkeys with multiple left arms, for example — will require such a remarkable amount of resources that I'm not sure if it'll measurably improve in the next year."}, {"date": "2024-06-03", "title": "The Rot-Com Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/rotcombubble", "quote": "Forty billion dollars later, the metaverse is no closer to existing, yet Zuckerberg keeps burning cash in the hopes that he can get just one more hit of hyper-growth."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "ChatGPT is a damned expensive product to operate, with the company burning through capital at a prodigious rate, and while OpenAI is aggressively monetizing it (both to consumers and to businesses), it’s far from crossing the break-even rubicon."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "And I’d argue that this is exceedingly dangerous for Silicon Valley and the tech industry writ large as executives disconnected from the process of creating software follow another non-technical founder hocking unprofitable, unsustainable and hallucination-prone software."}, {"date": "2024-06-17", "title": "Let Tim Cook", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/untitled", "quote": "To be clear, in most cases companies integrating ChatGPT pay on a per-thousand-tokens basis, meaning that OpenAI, while unprofitable, still generates revenue of some sort on each query."}, {"date": "2024-06-17", "title": "Let Tim Cook", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/untitled", "quote": "The Information reported last week that OpenAI’s annualized revenue may reach the billions in 2024, yet it remains deeply unprofitable, and even if Apple had paid money to integrate it, ChatGPT would still lose money on every search."}, {"date": "2024-07-01", "title": "The Shareholder Supremacy", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/tss", "quote": "Microsoft is run by Satya Nadella, another MBA that has, in his tenure, overseen layoffs of over 30,000 people, and pushed his company deep into the deeply unprofitable and unsustainable world of generative AI."}, {"date": "2024-07-01", "title": "The Shareholder Supremacy", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/tss", "quote": "They don’t care that the output is mediocre, that the product is unprofitable, that there is a quickly-approaching wall that generative AI can’t leap over as it runs out of training data, or that the transformer-based architecture of Large Language Models has hard limitations that are impossible to overcome."}, {"date": "2024-07-01", "title": "The Shareholder Supremacy", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/tss", "quote": "Generative AI is the next step up — a trend with an actual product, a superficially-impressive doodad that can sell cloud compute access and proliferate more software, even if the underlying technology is so remarkably unprofitable and unreliable that big tech firms are having to calm down their salespeople."}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "I feel a little crazy every time I write one of these pieces, because it's patently ridiculous. Generative AI is unprofitable, unsustainable, and fundamentally limited in what it can do thanks to the fact that it's probabilistically generating an answer."}, {"date": "2024-07-24", "title": "Rot Economics - An Interview With MIT's Daron Acemoglu", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/rot-economics-an-interview-with-mits-daron-acemoglu", "quote": "Because right now the thing I've been on about with generative AI is on top of not being super useful, it's so unprofitable."}, {"date": "2024-07-29", "title": "How Does OpenAI Survive?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/to-serve-altman", "quote": "SpaceX, while unprofitable, is (for better or worse) effectively tied to the US government as a necessary contractor, and has succeeded making billions of dollars in reducing its operating costs."}, {"date": "2024-07-29", "title": "How Does OpenAI Survive?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/to-serve-altman", "quote": "The Revenue, Cost and Market-Fit Problem As I've written repeatedly, generative AI is deeply unprofitable, and based on the Information's estimates, the cost of goods sold is unsustainable."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "These are stable, revenue-generating (yet unprofitable) ancillary players that likely will need to raise in the next 12 months."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "And a lack of creativity in the tallest towers of Silicon Valley and Redmond has allowed the richest men in the industry to be conned by a snake oil machine that loses billions of dollars."}, {"date": "2024-09-16", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/subprimeai", "quote": "These models are built by two companies that are deeply unprofitable (Anthropic is on course to lose $2.7 billion this year), and that have pricing designed to get more customers rather than make any kind of profit."}, {"date": "2024-09-16", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/subprimeai", "quote": "Based on how unprofitable they are, I hypothesize that if OpenAI or Anthropic charged prices closer to their actual costs, there would be a ten-to-a-hundred-times increase in the price of API calls, though it's impossible to say how much without the actual numbers."}, {"date": "2024-09-16", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/subprimeai", "quote": "And what we really don’t know is how unprofitable generative AI is for the hyper-scalers, because they bake those costs into other parts of their earnings."}, {"date": "2024-09-16", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/subprimeai", "quote": "Just “doing new stuff” has kind of worked for 20 years, in the sense that simply launching new stuff and forcing salespeople to hock it was enough to keep growth going, to the point that the tech industry’s leaders have bought into a truly poisonous and deeply unprofitable business."}, {"date": "2024-09-16", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/subprimeai", "quote": "What happens when the entire tech industry relies on the success of a kind of software that only loses money, and doesn’t create much value to begin with?"}, {"date": "2024-09-26", "title": "The Other Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/saaspocalypse-now", "quote": "As I hinted earlier, I see the enterprise and the SaaS market as the commercial real estate arm of the Subprime AI Crisis — an industry desperate for growth attaching itself to an unprofitable, unsustainable technology that they invested in in the hopes that it would fuel a decade or more of revenue growth."}, {"date": "2024-09-26", "title": "The Other Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/saaspocalypse-now", "quote": "Another deeply-worrying eventuality could be a race to the bottom, where growth-hungry SaaS companies either deeply discount or don't charge for AI, pushing their competitors to lower the price on their already-unprofitable products."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "Author: Ed Zitron OpenAI, a non-profit AI company that will lose anywhere from $4 billion to $5 billion this year, will at some point in the next six or so months convert into a for-profit AI company, at which point it will continue to lose money in exactly the same way."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "OpenAI loses money every single time that somebody uses their product, and while it might make money selling premium subscriptions, I severely doubt it’s turning a profit on these customers, and certainly losing money on any and all power users."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "As I've said before, OpenAI is unprofitable, unsustainable and untenable in its current form, but I think it's important to explain exactly how untenable it is, and I'm going to start with a few statements: - For OpenAI to hit $11.6 billion of revenue by the end of 2025, it will have to more than triple its revenue."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "ChatGPT’s free version is a poison in its system, a marketing channel that burns billions of dollars to introduce people to a product that only ten million people will actually pay for, and its future depends largely on its ability to continue convincing people to use it."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "Yet, once you get past these problems, you run head-first into the largest one: that generative AI is deeply unprofitable to run."}, {"date": "2024-11-01", "title": "The Cult of Microsoft", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-cult-of-microsoft", "quote": "At some point, these ugly messes will collapse as it becomes clear that their entire infrastructure is written upon increasingly-automated levels of crap, rife with hallucinations and devoid of any human touch."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "Microsoft, Meta, Amazon, and Google have all burned billions on the assumption that doing so would create something — be it a human-level \"artificial general intelligence\" or, I dunno, a product that would justify the costs — and it's become painfully obvious that it isn't going to work."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "Generative AI is incredibly unprofitable."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "Worse still, many of the companies integrating generative AI do so by connecting to models made by either OpenAI or Anthropic, both of whom are running unprofitable businesses, and likely charging nowhere near enough to cover their costs."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "The entire tech industry has become oriented around a dead-end technology that requires burning billions of dollars to provide inessential products that cost them more money to serve than anybody would ever pay."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "I sure hope they fix that totally unfixable problem. Even if it does, Anthropic has now successfully replaced...an entry-level data worker position at an indeterminate and likely unprofitable price."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "While it’s likely that these companies will fail due to inevitable organic realities (like running out of money, or not having a product that generates a profit), Musk’s enemies must now contend with a new enemy — one with the full backing of the Federal government, and that neither forgives nor forgets."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "We're two years in, and we have no killer apps — no industry-defining products — other than ChatGPT, a product that burns billions of dollars and nobody can really describe."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "Almost every single generative AI company that you’ve heard of is deeply unprofitable, and there are few innovations coming to save them from the atrophy of the foundation models."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "Yes, this much money can be this stupid, and yes, they will burn billions in pursuit of a non-specific dream that involves charging you money and trapping you in their ecosystem."}, {"date": "2024-12-16", "title": "Never Forgive Them", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/never-forgive-them", "quote": "Sam Altman is a con artist, a liar, and a sleazy carnival barker who would burn our planet to the ground, steal from millions of people and burn billions of dollars in pursuit of power, and I believe the same can be said of people like Dario Amodei of Anthropic and Mustafa Suleyman of Microsoft."}, {"date": "2025-01-17", "title": "The Slop Society", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-slop-society", "quote": "Newton said, and I quote, that he was \"taking detailed notes on all bloggers writing ’financial analyses’ suggesting that OpenAI will go bankrupt soon because it's not profitable yet.\" I do not like bullies, and I do not like threats."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "So, Why's Everybody Freaking Out? As I've written about many, many, many times, the Large Language Models run by companies like OpenAI, Anthropic, Google and Meta are unprofitable and unsustainable, and the transformer-based architecture they run on has peaked."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "After all, OpenAI loses money on every transaction — even its $200-a-month \"ChatGPT Pro\" subscription."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "If you ignore the hype, OpenAI and Anthropic are deeply boring software businesses with unprofitable, unreliable products prone to hallucinations, and their new products — such as OpenAI’s Sora — cost way too much money to both run and train to get results that, well, suck."}, {"date": "2025-02-11", "title": "What We're Fighting For", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/what-were-fighting-for", "quote": "Any discussion of ChatGPT should add that it lacks any real killer app and burns billions of dollars a year, and, I dunno, discuss how this thing doesn’t really have any real use cases?"}, {"date": "2025-02-17", "title": "The Generative AI Con", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/longcon", "quote": "What Are We Doing Here? OpenAI and Anthropic are both burning billions of dollars a year, and do not appear to have found a way to stop doing so."}, {"date": "2025-02-17", "title": "The Generative AI Con", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/longcon", "quote": "The Information — who I do generally, and genuinely, respect — ran an astonishingly optimistic piece about Anthropic estimating that it'd make $34.5 billion in revenue in 2027 (there's that year again!), the very same year it’d stop burning cash."}, {"date": "2025-02-17", "title": "The Generative AI Con", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/longcon", "quote": "Or that OpenAI, a company that has consistently burned billions of dollars, that has never shown any sign of making a profit, that has in two years released a selection of increasingly-questionable and obtuse products, actually runs out of money?"}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "On Unit Economics and Generative AI Putting aside the hype and bluster, OpenAI — as with all generative AI model developers — loses money on every single prompt and output."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "Nevertheless, OpenAI loses money on every single paying customer, just like with its free users."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "This is not an honest or reasonable way to evaluate the success of ChatGPT’s (still unprofitable) software business, because the actual metric would have to be divided paying subscribers by MONTHLY active users, a number that would be considerably higher than 400 million."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "In both of these scenarios, OpenAI loses money. - OpenAI's products are not fundamentally differentiated or interesting enough to be sold separately."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "If this were a \"real\" industry, other competitors would have similar scale — especially those run by hyperscalers — but as I'll get to later, data suggests that OpenAI is the only company with any significant user base in the entire generative AI industry, and it is still wildly unprofitable and unsustainable."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "These numbers aren't simply piss poor, they're a sign that the market for generative AI is incredibly small, and based on the fact that every single one of these apps only loses money, is actively harmful to their respective investors or owners."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "Its models, again like OpenAI, are unprofitable, unsustainable and heavily-dependent on training data that's either running out or has already run out."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "Stop it! For Perplexity, Who Cares? Perplexity, a company valued at $9 billion toward the end of 2024, has eight million people a month using its app, with the Financial Times reporting it has a grand total of 15 million monthly active users for its unprofitable search engine."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "Perplexity, like every generative AI company, only ever loses money, and its product — generative AI-powered search — is so commoditized that it's actually remarkable the company still exists."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "An unprofitable search engine?"}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "An unprofitable Large Language Model company?"}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "11 million monthly active users for its unprofitable, heavily-commoditized Large Language Model app is a joke — as are the 15.6 million monthly active users to its web presence — probably because it does exactly the same shit that every other LLM does."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "OpenAI and Anthropic are not real companies — they are free-riders, living on venture-backed welfare for an indeterminate amount of time because the entire tech industry has agreed to rally around the world’s most unprofitable software."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "This company has absolutely no path to sustain itself, no moat, and loses so much money that it will need more than $50 billion to continue in its current form. I don’t know how I’m wrong, and I have sat and thought a great deal about how I might be."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "This software is being forced on people at scale by corporations desperate to seem futuristic without any real understanding as to why they need it, and whatever use cases may exist for Large Language Models are dwarfed by how utterly unprofitable this whole fiasco is."}, {"date": "2025-03-03", "title": "Power Cut", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/power-cut", "quote": "In simpler terms, SoftBank is investing as much as $25 billion in OpenAI, then spending another $3 billion a year on software that only loses money, and still hallucinates, and shows no sign of getting meaningfully better or more reliable."}, {"date": "2025-03-03", "title": "Power Cut", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/power-cut", "quote": "To get the deal done, Microsoft changed the terms of its exclusive relationship with OpenAI to allow it to work with Oracle to build out further data centers full of the GPUs necessary to power its unprofitable, unsustainable models."}, {"date": "2025-03-03", "title": "Power Cut", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/power-cut", "quote": "In my opinion, the OpenAI-SoftBank deal is wildly unsustainable, dependent on SoftBank continuing to both raise debt and funnel money directly into a company that burns billions of dollars a year, and is set to only burn more thanks to the arrival of its latest model."}, {"date": "2025-03-03", "title": "Power Cut", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/power-cut", "quote": "I actually believe it will continue selling this unprofitable, unsustainable software, because the capacity it has right now is more than sufficient to deal with the lack of demand."}, {"date": "2025-03-03", "title": "Power Cut", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/power-cut", "quote": "SoftBank has committed to over $40 billion of costs that it cannot currently afford, taking on as much as $24 billion in debt in the next year to help sustain one more funding round and the construction of data centers for OpenAI, a company that loses money on literally every single customer."}, {"date": "2025-03-03", "title": "Power Cut", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/power-cut", "quote": "In fact, I think it’s time for everybody to seriously consider that big tech burned billions of dollars on something that nobody really wanted."}, {"date": "2025-03-17", "title": "CoreWeave Is A Time Bomb", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/core-incompetency", "quote": "Moreover, it’s a company that deals in the infrastructure aspect of AI, where one would naturally assume is where all the money really is — putting up the servers for hyperscalers to run their hallucination-prone, unprofitable models."}, {"date": "2025-03-24", "title": "The Phony Comforts of AI Optimism", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/optimistic-cowardice", "quote": "Generative AI has laid bare exactly how little the markets think about ideas, and how willing the powerful are to try and shove something unprofitable, unsustainable and questionably-useful down people's throats as a means of promoting growth."}, {"date": "2025-03-24", "title": "The Phony Comforts of AI Optimism", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/optimistic-cowardice", "quote": "OpenAI and Anthropic are abominations of capitalism, bleeding wounds that burn billions of dollars with no end in sight for measly returns on selling software that lacks any real mass market use case."}, {"date": "2025-03-24", "title": "The Phony Comforts of AI Optimism", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/optimistic-cowardice", "quote": "Last week, I covered the shaky state of AI data center provider CoreWeave — an unprofitable company riddled by onerous debt, with 77% of its $1.9 billion of 2024 revenue coming from Microsoft and NVIDIA."}, {"date": "2025-03-24", "title": "The Phony Comforts of AI Optimism", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/optimistic-cowardice", "quote": "Even if all of these things somehow happen, both CoreWeave and OpenAI are businesses that lose billions of dollars a year with no tangible evidence that this will ever change."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "The Information reported back in January that OpenAI was generating $25 million in revenue a month from its $200-a-month \"Pro\" subscribers (it still loses money on every one of them), suggesting around 125,000 ChatGPT Pro subscribers."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "As a reminder: OpenAI loses money on every single user. What Are OpenAI's Obligations? When I wrote \"How Does OpenAI Survive?\" and \"OpenAI Is A Bad Business,\" I used reported information to explain how this company was, at its core, unsustainable."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "Putting aside that each user is unprofitable, such remarkable growth — especially as it's partially a result of its extremely resource-intensive image generator — is also a strain on its infrastructure."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "In simpler terms, even if OpenAI wasn’t running out of money, even if OpenAI wasn’t horrifyingly unprofitable, it also may not have enough GPUs to continue providing its services in a reliable manner."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "OpenAI Has Become A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry OpenAI has become a load-bearing company for the tech industry, both as a narrative — as previously discussed, ChatGPT is the only Large Language Model company with any meaningful userbase — and as a financial entity."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "In the event that OpenAI cannot fulfil its obligations, CoreWeave will collapse. It is that simple."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "However, there is now a hard limit on how much of it there's going to be, both literally (in what's physically available) and in what Microsoft itself will actually OpenAI them to use, especially given how unprofitable GPU compute might be."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "In the present conditions, OpenAI is on course to run out of money or compute capacity, and it's unclear which will happen first."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "CoreWeave loses billions of dollars, OpenAI loses billions of dollars, Anthropic loses billions of dollars, and I can't find a single company providing generative AI-powered software that's making a profit."}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "Since I put out OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry, I've heard nothing in response, as was the case with How Does OpenAI Survive?"}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "That OpenAI is growing fast, and that somehow discounts the fact it burns billions of dollars and does not appear to have any path to making a profit?"}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "Large Language Models are boring, unprofitable cloud software stretched to their limits — both ethically and technologically — as a means of tech’s collapsing growth era, OpenAI’s non-profit mission fattened up to make foie gras for SaaS companies to upsell their clients and cloud compute companies to sell GPUs at an hourly rate."}, {"date": "2025-05-27", "title": "Desperate Times, Desperate Measures", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/measures", "quote": "It has no moat, its models are hitting the point of diminishing returns and have been for some time, and as popular as ChatGPT may be, it isn't a business and constantly loses money. On top of that, it requires more money than has ever been invested in a startup."}, {"date": "2025-06-30", "title": "Make Fun Of Them", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/make-fun-of-them", "quote": "The difference is that OpenAI has a consumer product that loses billions of dollars, and Lockheed Martin has products that makes billions of dollars by removing consumers from the Earth."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "I profoundly dislike the financial waste, the environmental destruction, and, fundamentally, I dislike the attempt to gaslight people into swearing fealty to a sickly and frail psuedo-industry where everybody but NVIDIA and consultancies lose money."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "Meta AI Revenue: $2bn to $3bn Capital Expenditures In 2025: $72 Billion Someone's gonna get mad at me for saying this, but I believe that Meta is simply burning cash on generative AI."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "Her argument, for the most part, is that Amazon was burning cash, had a ton of competition from other people doing similar things, and that analysts backed her up: Fair arguments for the time, though perhaps a little narrow-minded."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "We're three years in, and generative AI's highest-grossing companies — outside OpenAI ($10 billion annualized as of early June) and Anthropic ($4 billion annualized as of July), and both lose billions a year after revenue — have three major problems: - Businesses powered by generative AI do not seem to be popular."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "Those businesses that are remotely popular are deeply unprofitable..."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "and even the less-popular generative AI-powered businesses are deeply unprofitable."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "It’s also horribly unprofitable, and a sign of things to come for generative AI."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "Oh well. OpenAI and Anthropic Are The Generative AI Industry, Are Deeply Unstable and Unsustainable, and Are Critical To The AI Trade Continuing I haven't really spent time on my favourite subject — OpenAI being a systemic risk to the tech industry."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "To recap: - OpenAI and Anthropic both lose billions of dollars a year after revenue, and their stories do not mirror any other startup in history, not Uber, not Amazon Web Services, nothing. I address the Uber point in this article."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "The money isn't there, the users aren't there, every company seems to lose money and some companies lose so much money that it's impossible to tell how they'll survive."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "Large Language Models burn cash for negative returns to build products that all kind of work the same way."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "What I am describing is a bubble, and one with an obvious weakness: one company's ability to sell hardware to four or five other companies, all to run services that lose billions of dollars."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "Cursor Is A Systemic Risk To The AI Industry I know it sounds a little insane, but I believe that Cursor is the weak point of the entire AI bubble, and I’ll explain why, and how this could go."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "Anthropic raised its prices on Cursor so severely it broke its already-unprofitable business model."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "At best, it’s now acquired their own unprofitable coding environment and the smidgen of revenue associated."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "Get Acquired, Go Public, Or Die And that, right there, is Silicon Valley’s own housing crisis, except instead of condos houses they can’t afford with sub-prime adjustable rate mortgages, venture capitalists have invested in unprofitable, low-revenue startups with valuations that they can never sell at."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "I get people saying “they’re in the growth stage!” about a few companies, but when all of them are unprofitable, and even the unprofitable ones outside of OpenAI and Anthropic aren’t really making impressive amounts of money anyway?"}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "Anyway, long story short, these companies are unprofitable with no end in sight, don’t even make that much money in most cases, are valued more than anybody would ever buy them for, do not have much in the way of valuable intellectual property, and the two biggest players burn billions of dollars more than they make."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "Sorry, just to be clear, that’s the low end of what this would take to do, and they’ll have to keep doing it forever, until Sam Altman can build enough data centers to…keep burning billions, because there’s no actual plan to make this profitable."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "The revenue you see today is what people are willing to pay for a product that loses money, and I cannot imagine they would pay as much if the companies in question charged their costs."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "And let’s not forget Oracle, OpenAI, and Crusoe’s abominable mess in Abilene Texas, where Oracle is paying for the $40 billion of GPUs and Crusoe is spending $15 billion raised from Blue Owl Capital and Primary Digital infrastructure to build data centers for OpenAI, a company that loses billions of dollars a year."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "The complexity of these arrangements makes it hard to anticipate the full economic fallout if the cycle breaks down, but the systemic risk is building."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "Though the tech industry loves to talk about building a glorious future, its present is one steeped in rituals of decay and death, where the virtues of value creation and productivity take a backseat to burning billions and lying to the public again and again and again."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "If you say AI companies burn billions, they’ll say the cost of inference is coming down."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "It also massively subsidized the cost of rides — which is why prices had to increase — and spent heavily on driver recruitment, burning cash to get scale, the classic Silicon Valley way."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "Even Anthropic and OpenAI seem a little lethargic, both burning billions of dollars while making, by my estimates, no more than $2 billion and $6.26 billion in 2025 so far, despite projections of $5 billion and $13 billion respectively."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "Even if Anthropic was profitable — it isn’t, and will burn billions this year — a customer paying $200-a-month running up $50,000 in costs immediately devours the margin of any user running the service that day, if not that week or month."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "33 million dollars, all of it unprofitable, after it felt, at least based on social media chatter and discussing with multiple different software engineers, that Claude Code had become ubiquitous with anything to do with LLMs."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "Every article written about OpenAI or NVIDIA or Oracle that doesn’t explicitly state that the money doesn’t exist, that the revenues are impossible, that one of the companies involved burns billions of dollars and has no path to profitability, is an act of irresponsible make believe and mythos."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "The Information also adds that Anthropic “expects to stop burning cash in 2027.” This leaves two unanswered questions: - Where is the rest of Anthropic’s money going?"}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "How will it “stop burning cash” when its operational costs explode as its revenue increases?"}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "An optimist might argue that Anthropic is just growing its pile of cash so it’s got a warchest to burn through in the future, but I have my doubts."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "What I believe happened to Cursor will likely happen to every AI-native company, because in a very real sense, Anthropic’s products are a wrapper for its own models, except it only has to pay the (unprofitable) costs of running them on Amazon Web Services and Google Cloud."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "If Anthropic lets Cursor succeed, that’s revenue, but it’s also clearly unprofitable revenue."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "In any case, these costs seem to increase with the amount of money Anthropic makes, meaning that the current pricing of both subscriptions and API access seems unprofitable, and must increase dramatically — from my calculations, a 100% price increase might work, but good luck retaining every single customer and their customers too!"}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "I’m tired of watching these companies burn billions of dollars to destroy our environment and steal from everybody."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "I’m tired that so many people have tried to pretend there’s a justification for burning billions of dollars every year, clinging to empty tropes about how this is just like Uber or Amazon Web Services, when Anthropic has built something far more mediocre."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "After all, rumour has it that your deal with OpenAI — a company that burns billions of dollars a year — will involve it leasing your GPUs, which sure sounds like you’re doing vendor financing..."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "Both companies burn billions of dollars, and require an infinite amount of venture capital to keep alive at a time when the Saudi Public Investment Fund is struggling and the US venture capital system is set to run out of cash in the next year and a half."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "Is it because it’s unprofitable to provide it? And why, at this point in history, do we not know?"}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "That’s right, AI startups, all of which are deeply unprofitable."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "At some point, venture capitalists will be forced to stop funnelling money into unprofitable, unsustainable AI companies, which will make those companies unable to funnel money into the pockets of those buying GPUs, which will make it harder for those companies buying GPUs to justify (or raise debt for) buying more GPUs."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "During Broadcom's November earnings call, where Broadcom revealed that the $10 billion order was actually from Anthropic, another LLM startup that burns billions of dollars, which was buying Google's TPUs, and also booked another $11 billion in orders."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "I am skeptical of AI because everybody loses money."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "I believe every AI company is unprofitable with margins that are getting increasingly worse as they scale, and as a result that none of them will be able to either get acquired or go public."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Because all signs suggest that the current pace of funding must continue in perpetuity, as nobody appears to have worked out that generative AI is inherently unprofitable, and thus every single company is on the Silicon Valley Welfare System until everybody gives up, or the system itself cannot sustain the pressure."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "If even one of these companies falters and dies, the entire narrative will die."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "They lose so much money but folks we don’t worry about that, because they’re growing so fast."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "For AI data centers to make sense, most startups would have to start becoming direct users of AI compute, while also spending more on cloud compute services than they’ve ever spent. The largest consumers of AI compute are both unprofitable, unsustainable monstrosities."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Every part of the AI bubble — this fucking charade — is unprofitable, save for NVIDIA and the construction firms erecting future laser tag arenas full of negative-margin GPUs."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "What happens to OpenAI and Anthropic if their already negative-margin businesses when their customers run out of money?"}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "Unprofitable, unsustainable AI threatens future of venture capital, private equity and the markets themselves."}, {"date": "2026-02-26", "title": "On NVIDIA and Analyslop", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/on-nvidia-and-analyslop", "quote": "This is a big problem, because OpenAI needs $655 billion in the next five years to pay all its bills, and loses billions of dollars a year."}, {"date": "2026-03-03", "title": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-bubble-is-an-information-war", "quote": "I think it’s reasonable to ask whether NVIDIA might have sold hundreds of billions of dollars of GPUs that only ever lose money."}, {"date": "2026-03-10", "title": "The Beginning Of History", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-beginning-of-history", "quote": "Every AI startup is unprofitable, which means they need to raise money from venture capitalists, who raise money from investors that aren’t paying them, pension funds and insurers, and private equity and credit firms that raise money from banks, both of which will struggle should central bank rates spike."}, {"date": "2026-03-10", "title": "The Beginning Of History", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-beginning-of-history", "quote": "Need to justify unprofitable, unsustainable AI companies?"}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "As a result, based on my premium data center model, many data center projects are unprofitable even with a paying customer, and that’s assuming they even get built."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "Every single AI startup is unprofitable, and every AI startup functions by offering a service powered by AI models provided by AI labs."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "As the two largest customers of AI compute — there really isn’t even a distant third outside of xAI and hyperscalers, the latter of which are predominantly standing up OpenAI and Anthropic (or in Meta’s case a bunch of unprofitable LLM bullshit) — who’s going to pay for all of those data centers?"}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "Fucking Aquaman? The entire generative AI industry is based on unprofitable, unsustainable economics, rationalized and funded by venture capitalists and bankers speculating on the theoretical value of Large Language Model-based services."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "Both companies lose billions of dollars, both companies have no path to profitability, and both companies sell products — both to consumers and businesses — that simply do not work when users are forced to pay something approaching a sustainable cost."}, {"date": "2026-04-06", "title": "News: OpenAI CFO Doesn't Believe Company Ready For IPO, Unsure Revenue Will Support Commitments", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-cfo-news", "quote": "If your AI company always has to buy extra compute to meet demand, and said extra compute always makes margins worse, doesn't that mean that your company will either always be unprofitable or die because it buys too much compute?"}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "Saying it’s “the early days” also doesn’t really make sense when faced with the rotten and incredibly unprofitable economics of AI."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "Said data centers make up 90% of NVIDIA’s revenue, which means that 8% or so of the S&P 500’s value comes from a company that makes money selling hardware to people that immediately lose money on installing it."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "Every company loses money."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "And if it doesn’t make that much revenue — and also doesn’t get funding or debt to support it — OpenAI will run out of money, much as Anthropic will if that capacity gets built and it doesn’t make tens of billions of dollars a month to pay for it."}, {"date": "2026-04-21", "title": "Four Horsemen of the AIpocalypse", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/four-horsemen-of-the-aipocalypse", "quote": "OpenAI and Anthropic both burn billions of dollars a year, with The Information reporting that Anthropic expects to burn at least $11 billion and OpenAI $25 billion in 2026."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "Had users been forced to pay their actual rates, I imagine many would’ve bounced off the product immediately, as it’s very, very easy to burn through $5 of tokens if you’re fucking around and exploring what an LLM can do."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "Now, I should add that Google and Amazon are far-savvier and less-desperate than Oracle, meaning that they can take the hit if Anthropic ends up running out of money."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "I am genuinely asking you to seriously consider that one or both of these companies will run out of money."}, {"date": "2026-05-06", "title": "Am I Meant To Be Impressed?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/am-i-meant-to-be-impressed", "quote": "They know that if these companies die they’re going to lose billions of dollars of revenue, but that they also have to compete with them for fear that they’ll be seen as “falling behind” their horrible progeny."}, {"date": "2026-05-06", "title": "Am I Meant To Be Impressed?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/am-i-meant-to-be-impressed", "quote": "Every single AI business you see is unprofitable, nor do any of them have a path to break-even, let alone sustainability."}, {"date": "2026-05-12", "title": "Where Are All The Data Centers?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/where-are-all-the-data-centers", "quote": "In the end, the “proof” that SBF was rich and that FTX was solvent was that nobody had run out of money and that nothing bad had happened to anybody."}, {"date": "2026-05-19", "title": "AI Is Too Expensive", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-too-expensive", "quote": "Said capacity is mostly taken up by OpenAI and Anthropic, two companies that burn billions of dollars and do not appear to have an answer for how they might stop."}, {"date": "2026-05-19", "title": "AI Is Too Expensive", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-too-expensive", "quote": "This means that the current token spend you’re seeing is entirely experimental, which is why organizations keep burning through their tokens so fast."}, {"date": "2026-05-22", "title": "News: OpenAI Had A Negative 122% Non-GAAP Operating Margin In Q1 2026, and ChatGPT Growth Has Stalled", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/news-openai-had-a-negative-122-operating-margin-in-q1-2026-and-chatgpt-growth-has-stalled", "quote": "What’s clear is that we’re in an information war between two companies that burn billions of dollars, with one of them (OpenAI) allegedly planning to file for an IPO as soon as today."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "We are slaves to middle management and the middle management mindset, we are living in their world, and it will collapse because they never really understood anything to begin with."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "LLMs can do work-shaped stuff, sometimes, as long as you debase yourself to accept mediocre and often-broken stuff that you have to keep a vigilant eye on, and either use a subsided product that loses Anthropic money or pay a shit ton of money as an enterprise to Anthropic and it still loses money."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "Put another way, there’s barely a few billion dollars of demand outside of two companies that lose billions — or tens of billions — of dollars a year."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "If we assume that half of that gets built, that’s still $875 billion in annual revenue that will be needed to keep these data centers from running out of money as their margins are atrocious and they’re all paid for with onerous debt."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "In Uber’s case, it burned through its entire annual token budget in a single quarter, which led to its COO saying it was harder to justify spending money on AI tokens because it couldn’t show a link between that spend and a meaningful increase in useful features on Uber."}], "verdict": "Mostly correct, his strongest ground", "analysis": "His best-supported recurring claim. <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_unprofitable__c1\" data-tip=\"cat_unprofitable__c1\" href=\"https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai_docs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">OpenAI and Anthropic lose enormous sums</a>. <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_unprofitable__c2\" data-tip=\"cat_unprofitable__c2\" href=\"https://www.wheresyoured.at/news-openai-had-a-negative-122-operating-margin-in-q1-2026-and-chatgpt-growth-has-stalled/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">OpenAI ran a roughly negative 122 percent non-GAAP operating margin in Q1 2026</a>, and <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_unprofitable__c3\" data-tip=\"cat_unprofitable__c3\" href=\"https://finance.biggo.com/news/mRiPlZwBTwP6zY3HRxp-\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Anthropic's 2025 gross margins were near 40 percent, far below software norms</a>. The descriptive part is accurate and documented: these firms are deeply unprofitable and cash-hungry. The predictive 'will collapse' half is mostly still pending, and <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_unprofitable__c4\" data-tip=\"cat_unprofitable__c4\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/28/anthropic-raises-65-billion-nears-1t-valuation-ahead-of-ipo/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">both keep raising tens of billions</a>, so survival is not yet falsified.", "srcs": [["How much OpenAI spends on inference (Zitron, Nov 2025)", "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai_docs"], ["Burry accuses AI hyperscalers of boosting earnings (CNBC, Nov 2025)", "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/11/11/big-short-investor-michael-burry-accuses-ai-hyperscalers-of-artificially-boosting-earnings.html"]]}, {"id": "bubble", "label": "It's a bubble / will burst", "stakes": "S4", "scope": "bubble-timing", "count": 147, "instances": [{"date": "2024-03-18", "title": "Have We Reached Peak AI?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/peakai", "quote": "If the AI bubble pops, the entire tech industry will suffer as venture capitalists are once again washed out through chasing an unprofitable, barely-substantiated trend."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "Nakedly-evil data startup Palantir saw its stock pop thanks to mentioning the possibility of selling AI software to armies, announcing a month later that it had won a $178 million deal with the U.S."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "Another hallmark of a bubble is a high-revenue, negative-profit industry."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "The CEO of a $2.2 trillion company spent two hours spouting a mixture of tech specs and fan fiction to a crowd of sycophants, and the world lapped it up, ignoring the fact that triple-digit percentages of year-over-year growth are equal parts disturbing and indicative of a bubble."}, {"date": "2024-05-13", "title": "Expectations Versus Reality", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/expectations-versus-reality", "quote": "The AI hype bubble, as I’ve noted before, is one entirely reliant on us accepting the idea of what these companies will do rather than interrogating their ability to actually do it."}, {"date": "2024-06-03", "title": "The Rot-Com Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/rotcombubble", "quote": "When the bubble bursts, I imagine these firms will be absorbed by the massive tech companies that have put billions of dollars into them in exactly the same way that Microsoft absorbed Inflection, quietly hiding their shameful failures and repurposing the massive compute investments to bolster the already-existent cloud infrastructure."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "He will push OpenAI to grow and sell into as many industries as possible, a specious hype-man selling to other specious hype-men desperate to connect their company to an AI bubble inflated by Altman himself."}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "And yes, that sound you hear is the slow deflation of the bubble I've been warning you about since March."}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "While one can \"teach\" a generative AI what a billion images look like, AI does not get hand cramps, or a call at 8PM saying that it \"needs it to pop more.\" It does not have moods, nor can it infer them from written or visual media, because human emotions are extremely weird, as are our moods, our bodies, and our general existences."}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "And Jim, in no uncertain terms, thinks that the generative AI bubble is full of shit."}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "Covello ends with one important and brutal note: that the more time that passes without significant AI applications, the more challenging \"the AI story will become,\" with corporate profitability likely floating this bubble as long as it takes for the tech industry to hit a more difficult economic period."}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "LLMs are entirely different pieces of technology to that of \"an artificial intelligence\" in the sense that the AI bubble is hyping, and it's disgraceful that the AI industry has taken so much money and attention with such a flagrant, offensive lie."}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "If there were some secret way that this would all get fixed, wouldn't Microsoft, or Meta, or Google, or Amazon — whose CEO of AWS compared the generative AI hype to the Dotcom bubble in February — have taken advantage of it?"}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "I've been asked a few times what I think will burst this bubble, and I maintain that part of the collapse will be investor dissent, punishing one of the major providers (Microsoft or Google, most likely) for a massive investment in an industry that produces little actual revenue."}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "It's been eighteen months since this bubble inflated, and since then very little has actually happened involving technology doing new stuff, just an iterative exploration of the very clear limits of what an AI model that generates answers can produce, with the answer being \"something that is, at times, sort of good.\" It's obvious."}, {"date": "2024-07-16", "title": "Put Up Or Shut Up", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/put-up-or-shut-up", "quote": "The media seems nigh-on incapable of accepting that generative AI is a big, stupid, costly and environmentally-destructive bubble, to the point that they'll happily accept marketing slop and vague platitudes about how big something that's already here will be in the future based on a remarkable lack of proof."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "August 2, 2024 was Black Friday for the artificial intelligence boom, as a week of rough earnings from Big Tech led to what felt like the entire media industry to ask: is the AI bubble popping?"}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "CNN asked “has the AI bubble burst?” and The Atlantic suggested (several months too late) that the “Generative-AI Revolution May Be A Bubble.” The Financial Times reported hedge fund Elliot Management told investors that Nvidia was “a bubble,” and Bloomberg reported that Big Tech had failed to convince Wall Street that AI is paying off."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "In Pop Culture, I suggested that the first signs of the AI bubble’s collapse would be in the failure of a major — though, not operating at the same scale as OpenAI — AI company."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "To be clear, we’re not quite at the bubble popping yet."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "The bubble could stay inflated."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "If these companies can raise, they’ll keep the bubble inflated, though not forever."}, {"date": "2024-09-16", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/subprimeai", "quote": "I also — and this, perhaps, is something I haven’t focused on as much as I should have — want to highlight the potential human cost of an AI bubble implosion."}, {"date": "2024-09-26", "title": "The Other Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/saaspocalypse-now", "quote": "Much like the feared commercial real estate bubble, SaaS may see its own series of dramatic price cuts to its AI tools as a means of competing and showing growth to the markets...despite the costs staying the same, or possibly increasing."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "If OpenAI — which dominates with, I’d wager, at least a 30% market share — is only making $1 billion a year from selling access to its models, and at this stage in the massively-inflated hype bubble, there may not even be $10 billion of annual revenue from companies integrating generative AI into their products."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "While this bubble can continue coasting for a while, nothing about the OpenAI story looks good."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "As I pointed out in Burst Damage, introducing an advertising revenue stream would require significant upfront investment, both in terms of technology and talent."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "Once the AI bubble pops, there are no other hyper-growth markets left, which will in turn lead to a bloodbath in big tech stocks as they realize that they’re out of big ideas to convince the street that they’re going to grow forever."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "I’ll end with a quote from Bubble Trouble, a piece I wrote in April: I was right then and I’m right now."}, {"date": "2024-12-24", "title": "Thank You", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/thank-you", "quote": "and OpenAI Is A Bad Business, along with more opinion-analysis pieces like The Subprime AI Crisis and The Other Bubble."}, {"date": "2024-12-24", "title": "Thank You", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/thank-you", "quote": "Every single AI piece I’ve written this year - my biggest being Pop Culture \\- has been me trying to work out what the hell is going on."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "In short, the recent AI bubble (and, in particular, the hundreds of billions of spending behind it) hinged on the idea that we need bigger models, which are both trained and run on bigger and even larger GPUs almost entirely sold by NVIDIA, and are based in bigger and bigger data centers owned by companies like Microsoft and Google."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "As a result, the markets are panicking, because the entire narrative of the AI bubble has been that these models have to be expensive because they're the future, and that's why hyperscalers had to burn $200 billion in capital expenditures for infrastructure to support generative AI companies like OpenAI and Anthropic."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "The entire AI bubble was inflated based on the premise that these models were simply impossible to build without burning massive amounts of cash, straining the power grid, and blowing past emissions goals, and that these were necessary costs to create \"powerful AI.\" Obviously, that wasn’t true."}, {"date": "2025-02-17", "title": "The Generative AI Con", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/longcon", "quote": "The AI bubble means that effectively every single media outlet has been talking about artificial intelligence in the vaguest way, and there's really only been one \"product\" that they can try that \"is AI\" — and that product is ChatGPT."}, {"date": "2025-02-17", "title": "The Generative AI Con", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/longcon", "quote": "Despite the hype, the marketing, the tens of thousands of media articles, the trillions of dollars in market capitalization, none of this feels real, or at least real enough to sustain this miserable, specious bubble."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "This bubble will only burst when either the markets or the hyperscalers accept that they have chased their own tails toward oblivion."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "Google and Microsoft, and hundreds of other companies that will be hurt by the contagion of an AI bubble imploding, just as they were in the 2008 financial crash, when the failure of the banking system trickled down into the wider economy."}, {"date": "2025-03-03", "title": "Power Cut", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/power-cut", "quote": "I have been — and remain — hesitant to “call the bubble bursting,” because bubbles do not burst in neat little events."}, {"date": "2025-03-03", "title": "Power Cut", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/power-cut", "quote": "Why is it that tangible, meaningful evidence that we’re in a bubble — and possibly a sign that it has actually popped — is less interesting than the fact that Claude Sonnet 3.7 “can think longer”?"}, {"date": "2025-03-17", "title": "CoreWeave Is A Time Bomb", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/core-incompetency", "quote": "While it’s hardly a recognizable name — like, say, OpenAI, or Microsoft, or Nvidia — this company is worth observing, if not for the fact that it’s arguably the first major IPO that we’ve seen from the current generative AI hype bubble, and undoubtedly the biggest."}, {"date": "2025-03-24", "title": "The Phony Comforts of AI Optimism", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/optimistic-cowardice", "quote": "My core theses — The Rot Economy (that the tech industry has become dominated by growth), The Rot-Com Bubble (that the tech industry has run out of hyper-growth ideas), and that generative AI has created a kind of capitalist death cult where nobody wants to admit that they're not making any money — are far from comfortable."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "I have never won an award in my life, so help me win this one. --- Soundtrack: Mastodon - High Road --- I wanted to start this newsletter with a pithy anecdote about chaos, both that caused by Donald Trump's tariffs and the brittle state of the generative AI bubble."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "While OpenAI's capacity is sufficient, It does not have the resources available to easily handle bursts in user growth in a stable manner."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "The Future of Generative AI Rests On OpenAI, And OpenAI's Future Rests On Near-Impossible Financial Requirements I have done my best to write this piece in as objective a tone as possible, regardless of my feelings about the generative AI bubble and its associated boosters."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "It's Time To Wake Up Even in a hysterical bubble where everybody is agreeing that this is the future, OpenAI currently requires more money and more compute than is reasonable to acquire."}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "Let's talk about why this bubble actually inflated! So, let's start simple: the term \"artificial intelligence\" is bastardized to the point it effectively means nothing and everything at the same time."}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "This Bubble Was Also Inflated By The Failure of Google Search Everybody I talk to that uses ChatGPT regularly uses it as either a way to generate shitty limericks or as a replacement for Google search, a product that Google has deliberately made worse as a means of increasing profits."}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "One of the major warning signs that the bubble was bursting was big tech firms reducing their capital expenditures, a call I've made before, with a little more clarity, on April 4 2024: We're about to find out if I'm right."}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "Only an industry out of options would choose this bubble, and the punishment for doing so will be grim."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "The tech media has enabled every single bubble, without exception, accepting every single narrative fed to them by VCs and startups, with even critical reporters still accepting the lunacy of a company like OpenAI just because everybody else does too."}, {"date": "2025-06-09", "title": "Never Forget What They've Done", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/never-forget-what-theyve-done", "quote": "What’s particularly horrifying about the AI bubble is that it’s shown that when they decide to, big tech can put hundreds of billions behind whatever the fuck they want."}, {"date": "2025-06-16", "title": "Sincerity Wins The War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sic", "quote": "What’s crazy to me is that many of the problems with the AI bubble — as with the metaverse, as with the return to office, as with inflation and price gouging — are obvious if you actually use the things or participate in reality, but such things do not always fit with the editorial message."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "In short, I believe the AI bubble is deeply unstable, built on vibes and blind faith, and when I say \"the AI bubble,\" I mean the entirety of the AI trade."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "No, this isn’t gonna be a traditional guide, but something you can look at and say “oh that’s why the AI bubble is so bad.” And at this point, I know I’m tired of being gaslit by guys in gingham shirts who desperately want to curry favour with other guys in gingham shirts but who also have PHDs."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "This dominance is also why ordinary people ought to be deeply concerned about the AI bubble."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "In fact, this was just before the dot com bubble burst, and when optimism about the web was at a high point. Yet the comparison stops there — people obviously liked buying shit online, it was the business models of many of these companies — like WebVan — that sucked."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "My Rot-Com Bubble thesis suggests we're out of hypergrowth ideas, and yeah, I think we're out of ideas related to Large Language Models too."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "Well, okay, what he said was much worse: We are in a bubble."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "Everywhere you look in the AI trade, things get worse — no revenue, billions being burned, no moat, no infrastructure play, no comparables in history other than the dot com bubble and WeWork, and a series of flagrant lies spouted by the powerful and members of the press that are afraid of moving against market consensus."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "The only people failing to make their case are the AI optimists still claiming that these companies are making \"powerful AI.\" And once this bubble pops, I will be asking for an apology."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "What I am describing is a bubble, and one with an obvious weakness: one company's ability to sell hardware to four or five other companies, all to run services that lose billions of dollars."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "Author: Ed Zitron In the last week, we’ve had no less than three different pieces asking whether the massive proliferation of data centers is a massive bubble, and though they, at times, seem to take the default position of AI’s inevitable value, they’ve begun to sour on the idea that it’s going to happen soon."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "In any case, I think Cursor is a huge indicator of the current fragility of the bubble — and the fact that for most AI startups, there’s simply no way out, because being acquired or going public does not appear to be a viable route."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "Cursor Is A Systemic Risk To The AI Industry I know it sounds a little insane, but I believe that Cursor is the weak point of the entire AI bubble, and I’ll explain why, and how this could go."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "The closest they’ve got is using generative AI startups as beauty pageants for guys wearing Patagonia, finding ways to pretend that the guy who runs an AI startup — sorry, AI lab — is some sort of mysterious genius versus just another founder in just another bubble with just another overstuffed valuation."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "As I discussed at length in the Hater’s Guide to the AI Bubble, NVIDIA is the weak point in the stock market, representing roughly 19% of the value of the Magnificent 7, which in turn makes up about 35% of the value of the US stock market."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "As I’ve said again and again, the generative AI bubble is, and always has been, fundamentally irrational, and inherently gothic, playing in the ruins, patterns and pathways of previous tech booms despite this one having little or no resemblance to them."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "And, like the rest of the AI bubble, Silicon Valley’s only liquidity path out of the bubble is big tech itself."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "Again, I tell you, put aside any feelings you may have about generative AI itself, and focus on the actual economic results of this bubble."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "Although the stock market isn’t the economy, the two things are inherently linked, and the popping of the AI bubble will have downstream ramifications, just like the dot com bubble did on the wider economy."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "If anything, the massive amounts of capital have allowed us to massively condense the time in which a bubble goes from \"possible\" to \"bursting and washing out a bunch of people,\" because the tech industry has such a powerful follower culture that only one or two unique ideas can exist at one time."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "The \"fiber optic cable\" of this era is mostly owned by a few companies. 42% of NVIDIA's revenue is from the magnificent 7, and the companies buying these GPUs are, for the most part, not going to go bust once the AI bubble bursts."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Widespread access to \"cheaper GPUs\" has already happened, and has created no new use cases. As a result of the AI bubble, there are now many, many different vendors to get access to GPUs on an hourly rate, often for as little as $1 an hour."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "While they might be cheaper when the bubble bursts, does \"cheaper\" enable people to do stuff they can't do now?"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "As I said previously, ChatGPT has had probably the most sustained PR campaign for anything outside of a presidency or a pop star."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "To quote Merchant, “the drumbeat, marketing, and pop culture of ‘powerful AI’ encourages and permits management to replace or degrade jobs they might not otherwise have.” Across the board, the people being “replaced” by AI are the victims of lazy, incompetent cost-cutters who don’t care if they ship poorly-translated text."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "Mark Zuckerberg says we’re in a bubble, Sam Altman says we’re in a bubble, Alibaba Chairman and billionaire Joe Tsai says we’re in a bubble, Apollo says we’re in a bubble, nobody is making money and nobody knows why they’re actually doing this anymore, just that they must do it immediately."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "Today I will make the case that generative AI’s fundamental growth story is flawed, and explain why we’re in the midst of an egregious bubble."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "To understand the AI bubble is to understand why CEOs do the things they do."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "Outside of these two, AI startups are floundering, struggling to stay alive and raising money in several-hundred million dollar bursts as their negative-gross-margin businesses flounder."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "It is now inevitable that this bubble bursts."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "Every single “vibe coding is the future,” “the power of AI,” and “AI job loss” story written perpetuates a myth that will only lead to more regular people getting hurt when the bubble bursts."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "I’ve also recorded an episode about this on my podcast Better Offline (RSS feed, Apple, Spotify, iHeartRadio), it’s a little different but both handle the same information, just subscribe and it'll pop up."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "Back in June 2024, I wrote about the Rot-Com Bubble, and my greater theory that the tech industry has run out of hypergrowth ideas: In simple terms, big tech, Amazon, Google, Microsoft and Meta, but also a number of other companies, no longer has the “next big thing,” and jumped on AI out of an abundance of desperation."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "Once this pops — and it will pop, because there is simply not enough money to do this forever — there must be a referendum on those that chose to ignore the naked instability of this era, and the endless lies that inflated the AI bubble."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "What if all of this was utterly senseless?* As I wrote last year, the tech industry has run out of hypergrowth ideas, facing something I call “the Rot Com bubble.” In simple terms, they’re only “doing AI” because there do not appear to be any other viable ideas to continue the Rot Economy’s eternal growth-at-all-costs dance."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Nevertheless, the problem is that in any bubble, being really stupid and ignorant works right up until it doesn’t, and however harsh the dot com bubble might have been, it wasn’t harsh enough and those who were responsible were left unpunished and unashamed, guaranteeing that this cycle would happen again."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Investors have allowed themselves to be played, and the results will be worse than the dot com bubble bursting by several echelons."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Before then, NVIDIA’s bubble is likely to burst."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "These deals, while seeming like they’re trending positively, are both incredibly important to the future of the AI bubble, and any failure will spook an already-nervous market."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Every part of the AI bubble — this fucking charade — is unprofitable, save for NVIDIA and the construction firms erecting future laser tag arenas full of negative-margin GPUs."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Every single time the question comes with an undercurrent of venom — the suggestion that I’m being an asshole for daring to question the wondrous AI bubble."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "The AI bubble is an inflation of capital and egos, of people emboldened and outright horny over the prospect of millions of people’s livelihoods being automated away."}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "Power Cut, an early warning sign that the bubble was bursting as Microsoft pulled out of gigawatts of data center deals."}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble Volume 2: a massive omnibus summary of every major AI company's weaknesses - the pathetic revenues, terrible margins and horrifying costs, and how hopeless everything feels."}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "An interview with MarketWatch about The Hater's Guide to the AI Bubble."}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "A chat with Brooke Gladstone on NPR about the AI bubble."}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "My fear - and expectation - is that many people still do not realize that there is an AI bubble or will not accept how significant and dangerous the bubble is, meaning that everybody is going to act like AI is the biggest most hugest and most special thing in the world right up until they accept that it isn't."}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "Never forget (or forgive them for) what they've done to the computer, and never forget that those scorned by the AI bubble are legion. Join me on r/Betteroffline, you are far from alone."}, {"date": "2026-02-26", "title": "On NVIDIA and Analyslop", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/on-nvidia-and-analyslop", "quote": "If you want to know more, I wrote a long premium piece that goes into it (among the ways in which AI is worse than the dot com bubble)."}, {"date": "2026-02-26", "title": "On NVIDIA and Analyslop", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/on-nvidia-and-analyslop", "quote": "If anything changes here — such as difficulty acquiring debt or investor pressure cutting capex — NVIDIA is in real trouble, as it’s made over $95 billion in commitments to build out for the AI bubble."}, {"date": "2026-03-03", "title": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-bubble-is-an-information-war", "quote": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War Started By Two Companies — Anthropic and OpenAI — Who Use The Media To Mislead the Public and Investors I get that it’s difficult too."}, {"date": "2026-03-10", "title": "The Beginning Of History", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-beginning-of-history", "quote": "That is what brings us back to the AI bubble."}, {"date": "2026-03-10", "title": "The Beginning Of History", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-beginning-of-history", "quote": "Iran changes that in the most obvious way possible — if prices soar, interest rates may follow, and if rates go up, even by a point or two of a percentage, financing the tens and hundreds of billions of dollars in borrowing that the AI bubble demands will become significantly more expensive."}, {"date": "2026-03-10", "title": "The Beginning Of History", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-beginning-of-history", "quote": "As self-serving as it sounds, I really do recommend you read my premium piece about the AI Bubble’s Impossible Promises, because I laid out there how stupid and impossible gigawatt data centers were before the war in Iran."}, {"date": "2026-03-17", "title": "Why Are We Still Doing This?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/why-are-we-still-doing-this", "quote": "Okay, okay, I know why we’re doing it — the software industry is out of hypergrowth ideas and has been in a years-long decline since 2018, though it briefly had a burst of excitement in 2021 when money was cheap and everybody was insane after the lockdowns ended."}, {"date": "2026-03-24", "title": "The AI Industry Is Lying To You", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-industry-is-lying-to-you", "quote": "It helps support free newsletters like these! --- The entire AI bubble is built on a vague sense of inevitability — that if everybody just believes hard enough that none of this can ever, ever go wrong that at some point all of the very obvious problems will just go away."}, {"date": "2026-03-24", "title": "The AI Industry Is Lying To You", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-industry-is-lying-to-you", "quote": "Not to sound unprofessional or nothing, but what the fuck is going on? We have 241GW of “planned” capacity in America, of which only 79.5GW of which is “under active development,” but when you dig deeper, only 5GW of capacity is actually under construction? The entire AI bubble is a god damn mirage."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "When the AI bubble started, venture capitalists flooded AI startups with cash, encouraging them to create hypergrowth businesses using, for the most part, monthly subscription costs that didn’t come close to covering the costs."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "Fast-growing” AI companies only grew because they were allowed to burn as much money as they wanted selling services that are entirely unsustainable, raising more venture capital money with every burst of user growth, which they use to aggressively market to new users and grow further to raise another bump of venture capital."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "I will put you in the embrace of God, I swear. The AI bubble and its representative companies do not and have never represented the buildout of Amazon Web Services or the growth and burnrate of Uber."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "This point is trotted out by imbeciles to try and say “this is nothing like the dot com bubble,” which I fundamentally agree with — it’s worse!"}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "Any reduction in capex from big tech is a sign that the AI bubble is bursting, as NVIDIA’s continued growth only comes from Microsoft, Google, Amazon, Meta, Oracle and other large companies buying tens of billions of dollars of servers from Taiwanese ODMs like Foxconn and Quanta."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "Any problems with Blue Owl as an ongoing concern: Blue Owl is the loosest lender in the AI bubble, and if it falls behind on their loans or has issues with its limited partners, that’s a bad sign too."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "I can’t get over how weird the AI bubble has become."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "The AI bubble has every big, flashing warning sign you could ask for."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "Every month some new bullshit pops up."}, {"date": "2026-04-21", "title": "Four Horsemen of the AIpocalypse", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/four-horsemen-of-the-aipocalypse", "quote": "Soundtrack — Megadeth — Hangar 18 (Eb Tuning) For the best part of four years I’ve been wrapped up in writing these massive, sprawling narratives about the AI bubble and the tech industry at large."}, {"date": "2026-04-22", "title": "[Updated] Exclusive: Microsoft Moving All GitHub Copilot Subscribers To Token-Based Billing In June", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/exclusive-microsoft-moving-all-github-copilot-subscribers-to-token-based-billing-in-june", "quote": "It’s $70 a year, or $7 a month, and in return you get a weekly newsletter that’s usually anywhere from 5,000 to 18,000 words, including vast, detailed analyses of NVIDIA, Anthropic and OpenAI’s finances, and the AI bubble writ large."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "At some point investors — even the braindead fuckwits who have been inflating the AI bubble — will begin to question mounting R&D costs (which is where AI token burn is usually hidden) when the company’s revenue growth fails to follow."}, {"date": "2026-05-06", "title": "Am I Meant To Be Impressed?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/am-i-meant-to-be-impressed", "quote": "The magical hysteria of the AI bubble is such that Meta, Microsoft, Google and Amazon are, despite proving no actual profit from their AI investments, effectively protected by most of the media, investors and analysts."}, {"date": "2026-05-06", "title": "Am I Meant To Be Impressed?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/am-i-meant-to-be-impressed", "quote": "Sadly, asking the media or analysts to act rationally or apply any real scrutiny is a joke, because this is the AI bubble, where everybody is wrong because once everybody admits what’s actually happening they’re going to have to admit they’ve all sounded insane for years."}, {"date": "2026-05-12", "title": "Where Are All The Data Centers?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/where-are-all-the-data-centers", "quote": "Anyway, one of the most commonly-held parts of the AI bubble is that massive amounts — gigawatts’ worth — of data centers have both already been and continue to be built… …but then you look a little closer, and things start getting a little more vague."}, {"date": "2026-05-12", "title": "Where Are All The Data Centers?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/where-are-all-the-data-centers", "quote": "Considering how loud, offensive and conspicuous the AI bubble has become, it feels like we should have a far, far better understanding of how much actual capacity has been built."}, {"date": "2026-05-21", "title": "Anthropic's \"Profitability\" Swindle", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/anthropics-profitability-swindle", "quote": "Anthropic has deliberately leaked a quarterly “profit” where it knows it can suppress its costs, specifically made sure that the journalist gave it the out of “costs might increase,” and released it on the day of NVIDIA’s earnings as a means of keeping the AI bubble inflated."}, {"date": "2026-05-21", "title": "Anthropic's \"Profitability\" Swindle", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/anthropics-profitability-swindle", "quote": "This week, I’ll publish the second part to my ongoing series (“What If…We’re In An AI Bubble?”) about the factors and events that will cause the AI bubble to finally pop."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Salesforce, one of the most-prominent hypesters behind the AI bubble has spent millions of dollars on advertising and marketing to promote a product that doesn’t exist in the way that it’s being sold."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Hundreds of billions of dollars — at least $178.5 billion in America alone in 2025 — have been sunk into data center construction based on flawed information, astronomically more flawed than the assumptions that led to the dot com bubble bursting, as I covered in my premium piece from a few months ago."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Nevertheless, even the sweatiest, least-trustworthy boosters have begun to sneak in statements about “we’re probably not in a bubble,“ or “yeah it’s a bubble, but it’s a good bubble.” Jeff Bezos, when asked about the AI bubble, said that you “shouldn’t worry about it,” which…is not really sufficient, is it Jeff?"}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "The AI bubble is exactly that, a bubble, and like all bubbles, it will eventually pop."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "Over the last three weeks, I’ve published an exhaustive three-part guide to how the AI bubble might collapse, the events that might trigger it, and the consequences."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "People love to compare AI to the Dot Com Bubble (AI is far, far worse) because it’s much easier to rationalize bad behavior than accept that we’re facing the largest misallocation of capital of all time."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "The Dot Com Bubble was really two bubbles — one around eCommerce and internet startups, and one around telecommunications infrastructure."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "Per Justin Kollar, the telecommunications bubble grew because of a fundamental misunderstanding of demand: As a result, infrastructure was built far in excess of what demand existed, because most people weren’t online, and those who were had very slow internet connections."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "Every few days somebody makes a post like this suggesting that “the internet didn’t go away” and “railways didn’t go away” when their bubbles popped, but I think this is a fundamental misunderstanding of what AI is."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "Every part of this bubble relies upon the momentum of hype to substantiate every link in the chain."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "The only way to inflate the AI bubble both on a hardware and software level was to mislead the general public and investors on the costs and efficacy of AI models."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "This flimsy, half-assed logic is how the AI bubble got inflated in the first place."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "Thankfully, Bain did manage to publish one of the single-funniest quotes of the AI bubble: Put another way, the technology “worked (?),” but did not provide value in doing so."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "This was an opportunity for “journalist” David Faber to push back, and here’s how that went: This is how the AI bubble inflated! This is how it happened!"}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "When some of you are pushed to prove the ROI of AI, you immediately return to boring talking points about Uber, or the Dot Com Bubble, or some other slop fed to you by people actively conning you at this very moment. I mean this with as much empathy as I can muster: if you’re a huge AI booster, why do you defend this so vociferously?"}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "Over a three week period in May, I published an exhaustive three-part guide to how the AI bubble might collapse, the events that might trigger it, and the consequences."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "For something lighter, check out last week’s premium, where I re-introduce you to the antagonists of the AI bubble (and their fatal weaknesses) in caustic, slightly sweary terms."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "Last week I went on Bloomberg and discussed the state of the AI bubble with a clarity that rattled even the sweatiest boosters, mostly because I spoke with clarity about an investment frenzy whipped up through hype, deceit and mythology."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "After hearing a particularly colourful story from Kevin Smith, I came up with the perfect way to explain the AI bubble."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "One of my sources has come forward and brought me a story that will possibly burst the AI bubble."}], "verdict": "Mostly correct, but table stakes", "analysis": "He is probably right that there is an AI asset bubble, and he was early (2024) and sharper than the hedged CEOs. But this earns little credit, because <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_bubble__c1\" data-tip=\"cat_bubble__c1\" href=\"https://www.technologyreview.com/2025/12/15/1129183/what-even-is-the-ai-bubble/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">by late 2025 it was consensus: <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_bubble__c2\" data-tip=\"cat_bubble__c2\" href=\"https://www.technologyreview.com/2025/12/15/1129183/what-even-is-the-ai-bubble/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Altman</a>, <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_bubble__c3\" data-tip=\"cat_bubble__c3\" href=\"https://fortune.com/2025/10/04/jeff-bezos-amazon-openai-sam-altman-ai-bubble-tech-stocks-investing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bezos</a>, <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_bubble__c4\" data-tip=\"cat_bubble__c4\" href=\"https://fortune.com/2025/09/19/zuckerberg-ai-bubble-definitely-possibility-sam-altman-collapse/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Zuckerberg</a> and Pichai conceded it</a>, <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_bubble__c5\" data-tip=\"cat_bubble__c5\" href=\"https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2025/10/14/imf-says-ai-investment-bubble-could-burst-comparable-to-dot-com-bubble\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the IMF and BIS warned of it</a>, and 53 to 54 percent of fund managers agreed. The bare bubble call is the least distinctive thing he says.", "srcs": [["Everyone in tech agrees we are in a bubble (MIT Tech Review, Dec 2025)", "https://www.technologyreview.com/2025/12/15/1129183/what-even-is-the-ai-bubble/"], ["IMF and Bank of England warn of an AI bubble (CNBC, Oct 2025)", "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/10/09/imf-and-bank-of-england-join-growing-chorus-warning-of-an-ai-bubble.html"], ["54% of fund managers say AI is a bubble (BofA survey)", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/bofas-survey-shows-54-of-investors-say-ai-in-bubble-60-say-stocks-overvalued-4284842"]]}, {"id": "con_fraud", "label": "It's a con / fraud / lie", "stakes": "S1", "scope": "tech-viability", "count": 128, "instances": [{"date": "2024-04-29", "title": "Managing Up", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/managing-up", "quote": "Like ChatGPT, he’s a know-nothing that, through deterministic measures completely detached from the meaning of the underlying ideas, picks the right words to say at the right time."}, {"date": "2024-05-13", "title": "Expectations Versus Reality", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/expectations-versus-reality", "quote": "And when you really sit and think about it, the current AI hype cycle has done very little for society other than helping quasi-con-artists make millions of dollars."}, {"date": "2024-05-21", "title": "Sam Altman Is Full Of Shit", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-is-full-of-shit", "quote": "Sam Altman needs you to believe that AI will kill us all or going to destroy all our jobs and that he's a little bit scared of AI, because if you think for even a second about what this man is saying, you'll realize that he's not an engineer, he's a lobbyist and a liar."}, {"date": "2024-05-21", "title": "Sam Altman Is Full Of Shit", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-is-full-of-shit", "quote": "The AI reality distortion field feels like a giant con, used to keep media attention (and traffic) flowing to ChatGPT so that Altman can continue claiming that \"generative AI is the future\" when it's yet to prove itself necessary, essential, or capable of overcoming its massive energy, compute and training data needs."}, {"date": "2024-05-21", "title": "Sam Altman Is Full Of Shit", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-is-full-of-shit", "quote": "Artificial Intelligence is a watershed moment for the media, where liars and scammers and hucksters get rich every time that a fanciful claim is left untouched, and where products are built upon a foundation of stolen content interpreted by a model that doesn’t actually know anything — because AI can’t, by definition, know anything."}, {"date": "2024-06-03", "title": "The Rot-Com Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/rotcombubble", "quote": "Toner also added that Altman was caught “outright lying” on multiple occasions, and that two executives provided evidence of “psychological abuse” and lying and manipulative behavior on multiple occasions."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "On top of being an incredibly risky idea — borrowing money from a bank and putting it into an industry where the majority of companies fail — this is another example of how Altman’s cult of personality allows him to con his way through the world."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "Altman’s deceit was so severe that OpenAI’s board only found out about the launch of ChatGPT when it was announced on Twitter."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "These people are afraid of OpenAI potentially creating a computer that can think for itself at a time they should be far more concerned about the career-manipulator and con artist that’s running the company."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "Altman may not actually create anything, but he’s excellent at spotting market opportunities — even if these opportunities involve him transparently lying about the technology he creates while having his boosters further propagate said lies either because they don’t know or don’t care that Altman is full of shit."}, {"date": "2024-07-01", "title": "The Shareholder Supremacy", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/tss", "quote": "While she could've been lying, Murati rarely demonstrates any kind of technical depth, dancing around answers with the vaguest possible explanations, and if you're wondering why the host didn't push her at all, it's because he's Jeffrey Blackburn — a career manager at Amazon who recently joined DoorDash's board."}, {"date": "2024-07-01", "title": "The Shareholder Supremacy", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/tss", "quote": "Generative AI is the next step up — a trend with an actual product, a superficially-impressive doodad that can sell cloud compute access and proliferate more software, even if the underlying technology is so remarkably unprofitable and unreliable that big tech firms are having to calm down their salespeople."}, {"date": "2024-07-01", "title": "The Shareholder Supremacy", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/tss", "quote": "Mentally, it’s hard to consider any of this a grift, because doing so would be admitting how much of the economy is controlled by grifters."}, {"date": "2024-07-16", "title": "Put Up Or Shut Up", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/put-up-or-shut-up", "quote": "I hate to be that guy, but it’s all beginning to remind me of the nebulous roadmaps that cryptocurrency con artists used to offer."}, {"date": "2024-07-16", "title": "Put Up Or Shut Up", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/put-up-or-shut-up", "quote": "Generative AI's one real innovation is that it's allowed a certain class of scam artist to use the vague idea of \"powerful automation\" to hype companies to people that don't really know anything."}, {"date": "2024-07-29", "title": "How Does OpenAI Survive?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/to-serve-altman", "quote": "I fear for those founders relying on the current pricing for GPT and other models."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "Nvidia’s blackwell chips would help OpenAI models run faster and ingest training data faster, as well as — even if it’s not possible — fool investors into believing that OpenAI “had the latest tech,” letting Sam Altman keep the con going."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "The common thread between all of these events is that they’re all expressions of desperation, fear, and a total lack of confidence in the underlying profit."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "He cares about accumulating power, has been doing so for years, and will be back with another con within three years."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "And a lack of creativity in the tallest towers of Silicon Valley and Redmond has allowed the richest men in the industry to be conned by a snake oil machine that loses billions of dollars."}, {"date": "2024-09-26", "title": "The Other Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/saaspocalypse-now", "quote": "As a result, generative AI kind of felt like the perfect SaaS snake oil, a magical new way to indefinitely charge customers for the thing that they already should have."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "As I've said before, I believe there's also a subprime AI crisis brewing because OpenAI's API services — which lets people integrate its various models into external products — is currently priced at a loss, and increasing prices will likely make this product unsustainable for many businesses currently relying on these discounted rates."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "Worse-still, these models are all using effectively-identical training data (and they're running out!), which makes their outputs (and by extension their underlying technology) increasingly similar."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "At that point, OpenAI resembles a kind of investment scam where new investors exist only to help old investors liquidate their assets rather than anyone investing in the actual value of the company itself."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "Even then, OpenAI will have to both find ways to give developers more reasons to integrate its models while making sure that said models provide a service that the end-user will actually appreciate, which is heavily-reliant on both the underlying technology and the ability of developers to create meaningful products with it."}, {"date": "2024-10-14", "title": "You Can't Make Friends With The Rockstars", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/rockstars", "quote": "A complete abdication of one’s responsibilities, deferring to a man who has, time and time again, proven himself to be a chronic liar."}, {"date": "2024-11-13", "title": "Lost In The Future", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/lost-in-the-future", "quote": "On the other side of the tracks, Sam Altman is a liar who's been fired from two companies, including OpenAI, and yet because he's a billionaire with a buzzy company, he's left unscathed."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "Sam Altman has grown rich and powerful lying about how GPT will somehow lead to AGI, but at this point, what exactly is OpenAI meant to do?"}, {"date": "2024-12-16", "title": "Never Forgive Them", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/never-forgive-them", "quote": "Sam Altman is a con artist, a liar, and a sleazy carnival barker who would burn our planet to the ground, steal from millions of people and burn billions of dollars in pursuit of power, and I believe the same can be said of people like Dario Amodei of Anthropic and Mustafa Suleyman of Microsoft."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "Sure, they could con another couple of billion dollars out of Masayoshi Son and other gormless billionaires, but what’re they offering, exactly?"}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "It’s all been a con, a painfully-obvious one, one I’ve been screaming about since February 2024, trying to explain that beneath the hype was an industry that provided modest-at-best outcomes rather than resembling any kind of “next big thing.” Without “reasoning” as its magical new creation, OpenAI has nothing left."}, {"date": "2025-02-17", "title": "The Generative AI Con", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/longcon", "quote": "Dario Amodei — much like Sam Altman — is a liar, a crook, a carnival barker and a charlatan, and the things he promises are equal parts ridiculous and offensive."}, {"date": "2025-02-17", "title": "The Generative AI Con", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/longcon", "quote": "They are management consultants dressed as founders, cynical con artists raising money for products that will never exist while peddling software that destroys our planet and diverts attention and capital away from things that might solve real problems."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "I have had many people attack my work about OpenAI, but none have provided any real counterpoint to the underlying economic argument I've made since July of last year that OpenAI is unsustainable."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "OpenAI has the only meaningful userbase in generative AI, and this entire hype-cycle has been driven by its success, meaning any deterioration (or collapse) of OpenAI will tell the market what I've been saying for over a year: that generative AI is not the next hyper-growth market, and its underlying economics do not make sense."}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "Why does nobody want to talk about the underlying economics?"}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "You are being swindled! If Google replaced Google Search with Google Gemini it would have billions of monthly active users!"}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "Silicon Valley is dominated by management consultants that no longer know what innovation looks like, tricked by Sam Altman, a savvy con artist who took advantage of tech’s desperation for growth."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "We have merch. --- Last week, Bloomberg profiled Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella, revealing that he's either a liar or a specific kind of idiot."}, {"date": "2025-05-27", "title": "Desperate Times, Desperate Measures", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/measures", "quote": "It took four years for Amazon to sell 100 million Echo devices, Former NFT scam Rabbit claims to have sold over 130,000 units of its \"barely reviewable\" \"AI-powered\" R1 device, but told FastCompany last year that the product had barely 5000 daily active users."}, {"date": "2025-05-27", "title": "Desperate Times, Desperate Measures", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/measures", "quote": "OpenAI is a loser of a company run by a career liar that cannot ship product, only further iterations of an increasingly-commoditized series of Large Language Models."}, {"date": "2025-06-09", "title": "Never Forget What They've Done", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/never-forget-what-theyve-done", "quote": "There is nothing about an LLM that feels like it’s built to provide a real service, other than some sort-of fraudulent copy of something else lacking its soul or utility."}, {"date": "2025-06-09", "title": "Never Forget What They've Done", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/never-forget-what-theyve-done", "quote": "Sam Altman is a con artist that worked studiously for over a decade to accumulate power and connections until he found a technology and a time when the tech industry was out of ideas, and from everything I’ve read, it feels like he fell ass-backwards into ChatGPT and was surprised by how much everybody else liked it."}, {"date": "2025-06-16", "title": "Sincerity Wins The War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sic", "quote": "It’s media outlets that back up their workers, with editorial missions that aggressively fight those who would con their readers or abuse their writers, focusing on the incentives and power of those they’re discussing rather than whether or not “the markets” agree with their sentiment."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "To put it bluntly: Cursor's growth story was a lie."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "The term \"agent\" is one of the most egregious acts of fraud I've seen in my entire career writing about this crap, and that includes the metaverse."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "It has no path to profitability, and anyone telling you otherwise is a liar or a fantasist. Worse still, outside of OpenAI...what is there, really?"}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "The use of stories about models \"lying, cheating and stealing to reach goals\" or \"stop themselves being turned off\" are intentionally deceptive, as these models can (and clearly are) being prompted to take these actions."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "It also suggests that the actual underlying value of Windsurf’s IP was $250 million."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "By immediately applying old economics — the idea that you would pay a monthly fee to have relatively-unlimited access — companies like OpenAI and Anthropic immediately trained users to use their products in a way that was antithetical to their costs."}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "Though the tech industry loves to talk about building a glorious future, its present is one steeped in rituals of decay and death, where the virtues of value creation and productivity take a backseat to burning billions and lying to the public again and again and again."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "They’re your buddy, your boss, a man in a gingham shirt at Epic Steakhouse who won't leave you the fuck alone, a Redditor, a writer, a founder or a simple con artist — whoever the booster in your life is, I want you to have the words to fight them with."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "We don’t know if AGI is possible, anyone claiming they do is lying."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Ilya Sutskever and Mira Murati raised billions for companies with no product, let alone a product road map, and they did so because they saw a good opportunity for a grift and to throw a bunch of money at compute."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Also: if someone from “deep within the AI industry” has told somebody “big things are coming,” they are doing so to con them or make them think they have privileged information."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "And it was all a lie."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "That said, July, August, and September get a little weirder, because we’re relying on “almosts” and “approachings,” as I’ll explain as we go."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "If that’s the case, Anthropic is in real trouble - the cost of the services underlying its business increase the more money they make."}, {"date": "2025-11-12", "title": "Exclusive: Here's How Much OpenAI Spends On Inference and Its Revenue Share With Microsoft", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai_docs", "quote": "According to the documents, Microsoft received $493.8 million in revenue share payments in CY2024 from OpenAI — implying revenues for CY2024 of at least $2.469 billion, or around $1.23 billion less than the $3.7 billion that has been previously reported."}, {"date": "2025-11-12", "title": "Exclusive: Here's How Much OpenAI Spends On Inference and Its Revenue Share With Microsoft", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai_docs", "quote": "Similarly, for the first half of CY2025, Microsoft received $454.7 million as part of its revenue share agreement, implying OpenAI’s revenues for that six-month period were at least $2.273 billion, or around $2 billion less than the $4.3 billion previously reported."}, {"date": "2025-11-12", "title": "Exclusive: Here's How Much OpenAI Spends On Inference and Its Revenue Share With Microsoft", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai_docs", "quote": "Through September, Microsoft’s revenue share payments totalled $865.9 million, implying OpenAI’s revenues are at least $4.329 billion."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "NVIDIA is not Enron! Look, NVIDIA’s own memo said that “NVIDIA does not resemble historical accounting frauds because NVIDIA's underlying business is economically sound, \\[its\\] reporting is complete and transparent, and \\[it\\] cares about \\[its\\] reputation for integrity.” Now, I know what you’re thinking."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "Why is the largest company on the stock market having to reassure us about its underlying business economics and reporting?"}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "One might immediately begin to think — Streisand Effect style — that there might be something up with NVIDIA’s underlying business."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "It broke the law, it committed real deal, actual fraud, and NVIDIA is nothing like Enron."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "In fact, before NVIDIA put out a letter saying how it was nothing like Enron I would have staunchly defended the company against the Enron allegations, because I truly do not think NVIDIA is committing fraud."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "His wife, Lea, who also worked at Enron, received twelve months for conspiracy to commit wire fraud and money laundering and for submitting false tax returns."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "And because that’s happening, investors aren’t bothering to think too hard about the tech itself, or the deteriorating products underlying tech companies, because “these guys have always worked it out” and “these companies have always managed to keep growing.” As a result, nobody really looks too deep."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Venture capitalists would, of course, claim I’m insane, saying that the “growth is obviously there” while pointing to whatever startup has made $100 million ARR ($8.3 million in a month), all while not discussing the underlying operating expenses."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "The tech industry has run out of hypergrowth ideas, and in its desperation hitched itself to the least-profitable hardware and software in history, then spent three straight years lying about what was possible to the media, analysts and shareholders."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "I don’t care that you have heard developers really like it, because that doesn’t fix the underlying economic and social poison in AI."}, {"date": "2026-02-26", "title": "On NVIDIA and Analyslop", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/on-nvidia-and-analyslop", "quote": "Similarly, I make the effort to understand the underlying business models in a way that I’m not sure everybody else is trying to, and if I’m wrong, please show me an analysis of the financial condition of OpenAI or Anthropic from a booster."}, {"date": "2026-03-03", "title": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-bubble-is-an-information-war", "quote": "Worse still, NVIDIA’s earnings also mentioned $27bn in cloud commitments — literally paying its customers to rent the chips it sells, heavily suggesting that there isn’t the underlying revenue."}, {"date": "2026-03-03", "title": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-bubble-is-an-information-war", "quote": "While this is a somewhat-inexact calculation — we don’t know exactly how much compute was producing revenue in the period, and when new capacity came online — it shows that CoreWeave’s underlying business appears to be weakening as it adds capacity, which is the opposite of how a business should run."}, {"date": "2026-03-03", "title": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-bubble-is-an-information-war", "quote": "However, the way that OpenAI describes the AI industry sure does sound like a scam. It’s very obvious that neither OpenAI nor its peers have any plan to make any of this work beyond saying “well we’ll just keep making more money,” and I’m being quite literal, per The Information:"}, {"date": "2026-03-03", "title": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-bubble-is-an-information-war", "quote": "There’s also another possible answer: I think OpenAI is lying to the media, because it knows the media won’t think too hard about the numbers or compare them."}, {"date": "2026-03-03", "title": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-bubble-is-an-information-war", "quote": "that this company is clearly just…lying?"}, {"date": "2026-03-10", "title": "The Beginning Of History", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-beginning-of-history", "quote": "I am not stating that it is lying, but I do believe annualized revenue is a deliberate attempt to obfuscate things and give the vibe that the business is healthier than it is."}, {"date": "2026-03-17", "title": "Why Are We Still Doing This?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/why-are-we-still-doing-this", "quote": "If people were actually paying attention, they’d see the immediate problem: a data center takes an incredible amount of time to build, and takes longer depending on the amount of capacity necessary. It’s a deeply cynical con."}, {"date": "2026-03-24", "title": "The AI Industry Is Lying To You", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-industry-is-lying-to-you", "quote": "The fact that there’s so much data about data center construction and so little data about completed construction suggests that those preparing the reports are in on the con."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "If you are still saying this you are wrong, ignorant and potentially a big fucking liar. As I discussed about a month ago, Amazon Web Services cost around $52 billion (adjusted for inflation!) between 2003 (when it was first used internally) through two years after it hit profitability (2017)."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "This was an obvious con, a blatant subsidy, and a party that wouldn’t last forever."}, {"date": "2026-04-06", "title": "News: OpenAI CFO Doesn't Believe Company Ready For IPO, Unsure Revenue Will Support Commitments", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-cfo-news", "quote": "It's clear that both OpenAI and Anthropic are rushing toward a public offering so that their CEOs can cash out, and that their underlying economics are equal parts problematic and worrying."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "In any case, anytime that somebody tells you that we’re in “the early days of AI” has either been conned or is in the process of conning you, as they’re using it to deflect from issues of efficacy or underlying economic weakness."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "I would be concerned that Anthropic or OpenAI had lied to me, or that they were lying to someone else, and work diligently to try and find out what happened."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "Every AI startup has to raise hundreds of millions of dollars, and their products are so weak that they can only make millions of dollars of revenue after subsidizing the underlying cost of goods to the point of mass unprofitability."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "This entire industry has been sold on a lie, and as capacity becomes an issue, even true believers are turning on the AI labs."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "The con of the Large Language Model era is that any subscription you pay for is massively subsidized, and that any product you use can and will see its service degraded as these companies desperately try to either ease their capacity issues or lower their burn rate."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "As a result, customers of AI services have built workflows and habits based on an act of deceit."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "While for legal reasons I’ll stop short of the most obvious word, Anthropic and OpenAI are running — intentionally or otherwise — deeply deceitful businesses where their customers cannot realistically judge the quality or availability of the service long-term."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "And you’re a mark for untrustworthy con men selling software using deceptive and dangerous rhetoric."}, {"date": "2026-04-21", "title": "Four Horsemen of the AIpocalypse", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/four-horsemen-of-the-aipocalypse", "quote": "Government services are generally expected to be four 9s minimum, or 5 (99.999%) for more important systems underlying things like emergency services."}, {"date": "2026-04-21", "title": "Four Horsemen of the AIpocalypse", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/four-horsemen-of-the-aipocalypse", "quote": "Anthropic is a con, and said con is only made possible through endless, specious hype."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "Microsoft — like every AI company — swindled its customers by selling an unsustainable service, because it never, ever made sense to sell LLM-powered services on a monthly subscription."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "There’s also the underlying unreliability of hallucination-prone Large Language Models."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "Uber may have raised prices, but it didn’t have to dramatically change the underlying economics of the platform, nor did users have to entirely change how they used the product because Uber was suddenly charging them on a per-gallon basis."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "Yet that’s all part of the scam."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "I realize it seems a little much, but I genuinely believe that subscription-based AI services were an act of deception tantamount to fraud, as they misrepresented the core unit economics and thus the possibilities of a Large Language Model."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "AI is a con, and this is how the con works."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "It is unreliable, its economics don’t make sense, its outcomes don’t justify its existence, and the perpetrators of its con are boring, oafish and avaricious men disconnected from society and anybody who would ever disagree with them."}, {"date": "2026-05-06", "title": "Am I Meant To Be Impressed?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/am-i-meant-to-be-impressed", "quote": "Anthropic CFO Krishna Rao said in a sworn affidavit on March 9 2026 that its revenue was “exceeding $5 billion to date.” - I also at this point think that sources telling anybody Anthropic made $4.5 billion in 2025 alone were lying, as it doesn’t make mathematical sense otherwise."}, {"date": "2026-05-06", "title": "Am I Meant To Be Impressed?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/am-i-meant-to-be-impressed", "quote": "The story of massive AI demand is a lie — a trillion dollars annihilated to create the largest circle jerk of all time."}, {"date": "2026-05-19", "title": "AI Is Too Expensive", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-too-expensive", "quote": "We should make everybody who obsessed over theoretical ideas about what AI can or will do ashamed for their intellectual deceit or constant ignorance."}, {"date": "2026-05-21", "title": "Anthropic's \"Profitability\" Swindle", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/anthropics-profitability-swindle", "quote": "And as I’ve discussed before — and FlyingPenguin helpfully collated — adding up Anthropic’s previously-reported ARR from January 2025 to March 3, 3rd 2026 already gets us to around $6.66 billion."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "AI is a perfect storm of failed concepts and organizations, and the apex of the Era of the Business Idiot, an epoch where we’re ruled by people so thoroughly disconnected from the actual workforce that it was inevitable that a technology would be created specifically to grift them."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "And yet none of it’s really working, because Business Idiots don’t really know how anything works. LLMs Are Built To Coddle Losers As I said back in the original piece, think of The Business Idiot as a kind of con artist, except the con has become the standard way of doing business for an alarmingly large part of society."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Every single story about AI has to either directly gloss over the obvious financial and technological issues or start speaking in the kinds of vague theoreticals reserved for cults and multi-level marketing scams."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "I want to lead with a surprising comment: I don’t think LLMs, as a tool, are a grift."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "That being said, I think LLMs lend themselves perfectly to grifting."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Dario Amodei took this grift and perfected it."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Anthropic is a company purpose-built to con people into giving it by money by making people feel smart."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "The media was also primed for the grift."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "This is all it takes for somebody — a reporter or an executive — to extrapolate that because they were able to do something (even though the LLM did it), a subject-matter expert would be able to do even more. As a result, LLMs are fantastic tools for grifters."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "AI allows everybody to grow as long as everybody ignores the big, obvious problems with its efficacy and underlying economics. All you have to do is keep up the kayfabe that the problems aren’t problems and the solutions are imminent, or if you want to pretend to be a critic, you can also suggest that all of this is inevitable."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "This isn’t to say everybody making this argument is lazy, just that they’re unwitting pawns in a larger grift where mythology is used to support the biggest waste of capital in human history."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "And really, that’s the larger LLM grift: encouraging people to accept or sell lazy, half-baked shortcuts instead of fundamental units of labor or production, all while making them feel smart for doing so."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "AI data centers are themselves a grift, convincing investors that they’re backing large infrastructure projects akin to housing developments or factories, rather than warehouses full of expensive hardware for customers that may or may not actually exist."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Anthropic had to conspire with Elon fucking Musk to conjure up a single profitable quarter to swindle the media and its investors one last time."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Anthropic is either the single-most successful grifter of all time or speed-running a con where it fudges together numbers to raise endless amounts of money to keep its billion-dollar burn going."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "It is inefficient, power-intensive, environmentally destructive, and inherently sold based on things that it might do, providing far more value to scam artists and con men than it does to its end users."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "LLM Users Are The Victims Of A Con If AI had ROI, we’d be able to point with specificity to inarguable examples of economic impacts. AI boosters can jerk their binguses all they like about how Spotify’s CEO said its best engineers don’t write any code anymore."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "They didn’t raise hundreds of billions of dollars by talking about any product currently on the market, and that’s because the current products are not very good products. You are all the victims of a con."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "I’m also fundamentally unimpressed with anything I’ve seen an LLM do, because my requirement for software or hardware is that it works as advertised, and the very fundament of the AI con is that LLMs are sold based on their theoretical capabilities."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "Last week I went on Bloomberg and discussed the state of the AI bubble with a clarity that rattled even the sweatiest boosters, mostly because I spoke with clarity about an investment frenzy whipped up through hype, deceit and mythology."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "This is a hysterical era perpetuated by liars, cowards, imbeciles, craven boosters and the easily-fooled."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "Those excited about generative AI are either the victim or the perpetrator of a con centered around a technology to ingratiate at the highest cost possible."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "The only reason that we’ve been “doing AI” with such ferocity and veracity is that most companies are beholden to Business Idiots disconnected from production who have no real understanding of their underlying firms’ outputs, and thus have very little way of measuring them."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "Anyone claiming that you have to “measure AI’s ROI differently” is attempting to con either you or themselves."}], "verdict": "Overstated, and time is against it", "analysis": "His fraud reflex is a have-it-both-ways move, and the clock is running against it. In <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_con_fraud__c1\" data-tip=\"cat_con_fraud__c1\" href=\"https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">'NVIDIA Isn't Enron'</a> he explicitly writes that he does not think NVIDIA is committing fraud, then spends 15,000 sarcastic words mocking its denials and insinuating the setup is dodgy and unsustainable. That is insinuation with deniability, not an allegation, and <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_con_fraud__c2\" data-tip=\"cat_con_fraud__c2\" href=\"https://www.theargumentmag.com/p/ais-biggest-critic-has-lost-the-plot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">no major AI firm faces fraud charges.</a> The resolution cuts against him. A con collapses when the product fails to appear, but <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_con_fraud__c3\" data-tip=\"cat_con_fraud__c3\" href=\"https://technologychecker.io/blog/chatgpt-statistics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the product shipped and is used at scale,</a> <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_con_fraud__c4\" data-tip=\"cat_con_fraud__c4\" href=\"https://www.theargumentmag.com/p/ais-biggest-critic-has-lost-the-plot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the opposite of how Theranos or FTX ended.</a> Real overhype is not fraud, and four years of shipping has only widened that gap.", "srcs": [["NVIDIA Isn't Enron, So What Is It? (Zitron, Dec 2025)", "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it"], ["Burry accuses AI hyperscalers of boosting earnings (CNBC, Nov 2025)", "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/11/11/big-short-investor-michael-burry-accuses-ai-hyperscalers-of-artificially-boosting-earnings.html"], ["ChatGPT statistics: ~900M weekly users, ~25B ARR (2026)", "https://technologychecker.io/blog/chatgpt-statistics"]]}, {"id": "hallucinations", "label": "Hallucinations / unreliable", "stakes": "S1", "scope": "tech-viability", "count": 82, "instances": [{"date": "2023-08-03", "title": "The Age Of Mediocrity", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-age-of-mediocrity", "quote": "It doesn’t matter that the quality is questionable, inaccurate, or flat-out bad."}, {"date": "2023-08-03", "title": "The Age Of Mediocrity", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-age-of-mediocrity", "quote": "Executives are gung-ho about the prospect of automating every appreciable part of a business, adopting AI - which hallucinates regularly and is somehow getting worse \\- as fast as possible, regardless of whether it actually makes sense."}, {"date": "2023-08-03", "title": "The Age Of Mediocrity", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-age-of-mediocrity", "quote": "Perhaps another healthcare-adjacent company has to pull down the chatbot it installed to replace workers because it gave harmful advice, or Wendy’s drive-thru chatbot ends up giving away millions of free burgers because of an errant bug or hallucination."}, {"date": "2023-11-20", "title": "Sam Altman, Freed", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-freed", "quote": "While AI making goofy factual errors can be good for a laugh, but when poorly-tested (or error-prone) artificial intelligence enters critical infrastructure like healthcare, the results could be deadly."}, {"date": "2024-02-19", "title": "Subprime Intelligence", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-fried", "quote": "Even Microsoft struggled to find compelling use cases for their $7m AI Superbowl commercial, and these use cases are even narrower once you realize that generative video is so much more restrained by its hallucinations."}, {"date": "2024-02-19", "title": "Subprime Intelligence", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-fried", "quote": "A Wall Street Journal article from mid-February told a worrying tale of OpenAI and Anthropic — the two largest AI companies — racing to sell their generative AI systems despite the prevalence of hallucinations, and how few answers they had for applications that were highly regulated or dealt with highly sensitive data."}, {"date": "2024-02-19", "title": "Subprime Intelligence", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-fried", "quote": "And there are so many stories about how unreliable this technology is."}, {"date": "2024-02-19", "title": "Subprime Intelligence", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-fried", "quote": "Fortune reported a researcher's study into Large Language Models' ability to understand SEC filings and found that many of them were regularly either unable to answer or hallucinating incorrect information, with Meta's Llama2 model getting 70% of the study's questions wrong."}, {"date": "2024-02-19", "title": "Subprime Intelligence", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-fried", "quote": "Tech's largest cash cow since the cloud computing boom of the 2000s is based on a technology that is impossibly unreliable, a technology with a potent inverted Midas touch that burns far more money than it makes."}, {"date": "2024-03-18", "title": "Have We Reached Peak AI?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/peakai", "quote": "A study from Boston Consulting Group found that consultants that \"solved business problems with OpenAI's GPT-4\" performed 23% worse than those who didn't use it, even when the consultant was warned about the limitations of generative AI and the risk of hallucinations."}, {"date": "2024-03-18", "title": "Have We Reached Peak AI?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/peakai", "quote": "While Joanna Stern may have said that Sora's generative video clips \"freaked her out,\" much of what makes them scary is the assumption that OpenAI will fix hallucinations, something that the company has categorically failed to do."}, {"date": "2024-03-18", "title": "Have We Reached Peak AI?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/peakai", "quote": "As I've written before, hallucinations are a feature not a bug."}, {"date": "2024-03-18", "title": "Have We Reached Peak AI?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/peakai", "quote": "Hallucinations are not going away."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "In essence, the AI boom requires more high-quality data than currently exists to progress past the point we're currently at, which is one where the outputs of generative AI are deeply unreliable."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "The consistent hallucinations (IE: visual errors) you see in OpenAI's DALL-E (image) and Sora (video) products can only be improved (note that I didn't say \"fixed\") with a great deal more data, and there's much, much less of it online."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "There is, of course, one blatantly obvious problem: generative AI models are prone to hallucinations when using human data."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "As I've discussed before, today's models are rife with hallucinations that make integrating them actively dangerous for many businesses, and the only way to have fewer hallucinations is to give the models more compute power to process and analyze data, a dwindling resource that AI is actively helping to destroy."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "And when you cut through the hype, the AI industry is investing hundreds of billions of dollars to build infrastructure for a future that may never arrive based on the vague promise of hallucination-prone models."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "They seem far more willing to dream of the future than reckon with the consequences of a present where AI-generated code hallucinates references to non-existent software packages, allowing bad actors to create packages matching the made-up names to trick developers into integrating malware into their code."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "Running Sora is likely deeply unprofitable, and reducing its generative hallucinations — monkeys with multiple left arms, for example — will require such a remarkable amount of resources that I'm not sure if it'll measurably improve in the next year."}, {"date": "2024-04-15", "title": "They're Looting The Internet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-great-looting-of-the-internet", "quote": "LLMs also tend to hallucinate, a virtually-unsolvable problem where they authoritatively make incorrect statements that creates horrifying results in generative art and renders them too unreliable for any kind of mission critical work."}, {"date": "2024-04-15", "title": "They're Looting The Internet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-great-looting-of-the-internet", "quote": "Google can't find a way to make money off of its generative search product (which still, by the way, hallucinates) and is thinking about charging for it — the actions of a company that knows that none of this generative nonsense actually matters."}, {"date": "2024-05-13", "title": "Expectations Versus Reality", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/expectations-versus-reality", "quote": "Sora, much like other generative AI products, suffers from an imprecision and unreliability caused by hallucinations — an unavoidable result of using mathematics to generate stuff — and massive power and compute requirements that are, at this time, prohibitively expensive for any kind of at-scale usage."}, {"date": "2024-05-13", "title": "Expectations Versus Reality", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/expectations-versus-reality", "quote": "To make Sora kind of useful, OpenAI will have to find a way to dramatically increase the precision of prompts, reduce hallucinations to almost nothing, and vastly increase processing power across the board."}, {"date": "2024-05-13", "title": "Expectations Versus Reality", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/expectations-versus-reality", "quote": "Generative AI hallucinates because it doesn’t have a consciousness or any ability to learn or know anything."}, {"date": "2024-05-13", "title": "Expectations Versus Reality", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/expectations-versus-reality", "quote": "AI agents are error-prone, and the likelihood of failure in an automated task like moving a calendar invite or ordering an Uber is exponentially higher and less tolerable in a consumer setting."}, {"date": "2024-06-03", "title": "The Rot-Com Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/rotcombubble", "quote": "Have they made these things cheaper, or more efficient, or found a way to eliminate hallucinations?"}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "Shortly thereafter, former OpenAI board member Helen Toner revealed that Altman was fired from OpenAI because of a regular pattern of deception, where Altman would give inaccurate info about the company’s safety processes on multiple occasions."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "And I’d argue that this is exceedingly dangerous for Silicon Valley and the tech industry writ large as executives disconnected from the process of creating software follow another non-technical founder hocking unprofitable, unsustainable and hallucination-prone software."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "It doesn’t matter that Google Search is still plagued with nonsensical AI answers that sometimes steal other people’s work, or that the AI legal research tools being sold to firms regularly hallucinate — a problem that’s impossible to fix — because AI is the new thing that can be sold to the markets."}, {"date": "2024-07-01", "title": "The Shareholder Supremacy", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/tss", "quote": "It doesn’t matter that Google Search is incredibly broken as a result of Google’s constant drive to increase revenue, or that Google has decided to generate results on search using unreliable generative artificial intelligence that generates ridiculous answers."}, {"date": "2024-07-01", "title": "The Shareholder Supremacy", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/tss", "quote": "Generative AI is the next step up — a trend with an actual product, a superficially-impressive doodad that can sell cloud compute access and proliferate more software, even if the underlying technology is so remarkably unprofitable and unreliable that big tech firms are having to calm down their salespeople."}, {"date": "2024-07-16", "title": "Put Up Or Shut Up", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/put-up-or-shut-up", "quote": "Where is OpenAI's investment in mitigating or avoiding hallucinations?"}, {"date": "2024-07-24", "title": "Rot Economics - An Interview With MIT's Daron Acemoglu", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/rot-economics-an-interview-with-mits-daron-acemoglu", "quote": "And it feels like these core issues of hallucinations almost kill the concept of automation with generative. Yeah, exactly."}, {"date": "2024-07-29", "title": "How Does OpenAI Survive?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/to-serve-altman", "quote": "These models have utility, despite the propensity of these models to \"hallucinate\" (authoritatively state something that isn't true, or generate hands with too many fingers), and people are finding useful things for them to do, particularly in finance."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "Doing so will only cause more problems — there isn’t a chance in hell that Sora is profitable, and I’m fairly sure it’s even more expensive to run than ChatGPT, and I imagine its visual inconsistencies and hallucinations would make for some entertaining content for YouTubers and tech reporters."}, {"date": "2024-09-16", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/subprimeai", "quote": "By its own admission, OpenAI has heard reports that o1 is more prone to hallucinations than GPT-4o, and is less inclined to admit when it doesn’t have the answer to a question when compared to other previous models."}, {"date": "2024-09-16", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/subprimeai", "quote": "This is because, despite there being a model that checks its work, the work-checking part of the model is still capable of hallucinations."}, {"date": "2024-09-26", "title": "The Other Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/saaspocalypse-now", "quote": "No, you have to upgrade to Salesforce's $500-a-user-month \"Einstein 1 Sales\" product, billed annually, to quickly ask a generative chatbot what it is you're meant to be doing and hope that it doesn't hallucinate, or \"confidently lie\" as Salesforce product executive Patrick Stokes said earlier in the year."}, {"date": "2024-09-26", "title": "The Other Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/saaspocalypse-now", "quote": "Hallucinations are not a bug, so much as a feature of the transformer model that underpins generative AI."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "Perhaps it’s the hallucination problem, or perhaps it’s just that generative AI isn’t something that produces particularly-interesting interactions with a user."}, {"date": "2024-11-01", "title": "The Cult of Microsoft", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-cult-of-microsoft", "quote": "When a source ran the query multiple times, it hallucinated wildly different statistics for the same metrics."}, {"date": "2024-11-01", "title": "The Cult of Microsoft", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-cult-of-microsoft", "quote": "To be extremely blunt: Microsoft is asking its employees to draft their performance reviews based on the outputs of generative AI models — the same ones underpinning ChatGPT — that are prone to hallucination."}, {"date": "2024-11-01", "title": "The Cult of Microsoft", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-cult-of-microsoft", "quote": "At some point, these ugly messes will collapse as it becomes clear that their entire infrastructure is written upon increasingly-automated levels of crap, rife with hallucinations and devoid of any human touch."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "The hallucination problem is one that is nowhere closer to being solved — and, at least with the current technology — may never go away, and it makes it a non-starter for a great many business tasks, where you need a high level of reliability."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "While Anthropic's demo of its model allegedly controlling a few browser windows with a prompt might have seemed impressive to credulous people like Casey Newton, these were controlled demos which Anthropic added were \"slow\" and \"made lots of mistakes.\" Hey, almost like it's hallucinating!"}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "Or, for that matter, whether ads would provide a perverse incentive for OpenAI to enshittify an already unreliable product."}, {"date": "2024-12-16", "title": "Never Forgive Them", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/never-forgive-them", "quote": "This stuff — websites that state falsehoods because an AI hallucinated, or fake pictures of mushrooms and dogs that now dominate Google Images — is not going away."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "If you ignore the hype, OpenAI and Anthropic are deeply boring software businesses with unprofitable, unreliable products prone to hallucinations, and their new products — such as OpenAI’s Sora — cost way too much money to both run and train to get results that, well, suck."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "It was all flimflam to cover up how mediocre and unreliable the fundament of the supposed “AI revolution” really was."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "Moreover, OpenAI (like every other generative AI model developer) is incapable of solving the critical flaw with ChatGPT, namely its tendency to hallucinate — where it asserts something to be true, when it isn’t."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "Case in point: A BBC investigation just found that half of all AI-generated news articles have some kind of “significant” issue, whether that be hallucinated facts, editorialization, or references to outdated information."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "And the reason why OpenAI hasn’t fixed the hallucination problem isn’t because it doesn’t want to, but because it can’t."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "Operator uses OpenAI's \" Computer-Using Agent (CUA),\" which combines OpenAI's models with virtual machines that take distinct actions on web pages in an extremely-unreliable way."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "Again, that’s a very fuzzy — and unreliable — metric."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "This is closer to “the truth,” other than the fact it’s so unreliable as to be disqualifying, and the tasks it succeeds at (like searching on Tripadvisor) are remarkably simple."}, {"date": "2025-03-03", "title": "Power Cut", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/power-cut", "quote": "In simpler terms, SoftBank is investing as much as $25 billion in OpenAI, then spending another $3 billion a year on software that only loses money, and still hallucinates, and shows no sign of getting meaningfully better or more reliable."}, {"date": "2025-03-17", "title": "CoreWeave Is A Time Bomb", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/core-incompetency", "quote": "Moreover, it’s a company that deals in the infrastructure aspect of AI, where one would naturally assume is where all the money really is — putting up the servers for hyperscalers to run their hallucination-prone, unprofitable models."}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "But Ed, look at o-3: Oh you mean the new and extremely expensive reasoning model that hallucinates more somehow?"}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "They still hallucinate."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Is it because we've handed our economy to men that get paid $79 million a year to do a job they can't seem to describe, and even that, they would sooner offload to a bunch of unreliable AI models than actually do?"}, {"date": "2025-06-16", "title": "Sincerity Wins The War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sic", "quote": "The one using generative AI models that hallucinate, like every other LLM?"}, {"date": "2025-06-16", "title": "Sincerity Wins The War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sic", "quote": "What will an LLM — an inconsistent and unreliable generative AI system — do in a combat situation, and will a soldier trust it again after its first fuckup?"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Thomas Ptacek’s “My AI Skeptic Friends Are All Nuts” was catnip for boosters, a software engineer using technical terms like “interact with Git” and “MCP,” vague charts, and, of course, an extremely vague statement that says hallucinations aren’t a problem: Is it?"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "It resembles the death of the art of technology — inconsistent and unreliable by definition, inefficient by design, financially ruinous, and ADDS to the cognitive load of the user by requiring them to be ever-vigilant."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "While everybody (reasonably!) harps on about hallucinations — which, to remind you, is when a model authoritatively states something that isn’t true — but the truth is far more complex, and far worse than it seems."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "A “hallucination” isn’t just when these models say something that isn’t true."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "In reality, LLMs can generate code, and do some software engineering-adjacent tasks, but, like all Large Language Models, break down and go totally insane, hallucinating more as the tasks get more complex."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "Large Language Models are limited, AI agents are a pipedream and simply do not work, AI-powered products are unreliable and coding LLMs make developers slower, and the cost of inference — the way in which a model produces its output — keeps going up."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Large Language Models do not create novel concepts, they are inconsistent and unreliable, and even the “good” things they do vary wildly thanks to the dramatic variance of a giant probability machine."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "What use is a tool that gets more unreliable to access and expensive over time?"}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "But in reality, it’s just further compute-intensive ways of trying to fit a square peg in a round hole, by which I mean having a hallucination-prone chatbot do actual work."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "LLMs will always hallucinate, their outputs are not trustworthy as a result, they cannot be deterministic, and any chance of any mistakes of any kind are unforgivable."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "These aren’t “agents.” “Agents” makes it sound like there’s some sort of futuristic autonomous presence rather than a chatbot that’s looking at documents using technology that’s guaranteed to hallucinate incorrect information."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "As I’ve said for years, AI companies are inherently unsustainable due to the unreliable and inconsistent outputs of Large Language Models and the incredible costs of providing the services."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "There’s also the underlying unreliability of hallucination-prone Large Language Models."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "I mean, you can, but if you don’t prompt it right, understand how it works, or make a mistake in whatever you feed it, or if it just gets things wrong, it’ll spit out something you don’t like, which in turn means you’ll need to prompt it again."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "It is unreliable, its economics don’t make sense, its outcomes don’t justify its existence, and the perpetrators of its con are boring, oafish and avaricious men disconnected from society and anybody who would ever disagree with them."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "When somebody badmouths AI, the Business Idiot must defend it with everything they have, because attacking LLMs is attacking the output of an LLM, which is in turn a judgment on those who are tolerant of its mediocrity and impossible-to-avoid hallucinations."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "That’s because, as I’ve said before, nobody can actually measure the ROI of AI, or even create a standard measurement of the cost of a task thanks to the inevitable hallucination-prone nature of LLMs and the ever-growing list of different harnesses and “agentic” (sigh) interfaces."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "Every frothy hype-piece you’ve read has been written by somebody who has been conned into ignoring the true cost of AI, all in service of spreading a technology that’s unreliable, inconsistent and expensive at its core, and never, ever seems to get cheaper."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "Four years and a trillion dollars in, AI is more expensive, its companies more cash-intensive, its products just as unreliable, and its boosters more desperate than ever to make you ignore reality as a means of empowering one of a few ultra-rich oafs."}], "verdict": "Real, but the inference is a category error", "analysis": "Directionally right about a real problem, wrong about its scope and trajectory. Reliability in 2026 is bimodal. Unsupervised on the open web it is genuinely bad: AI search wrong on 60 percent of news queries, legal AI hallucinating 17 to 33 percent. Grounded and verifiable it is genuinely good: under 1.5 percent on the best systems. His move from 'it hallucinates' to 'therefore untrustworthy and useless' is the error. The right standard is the fallible human, not perfection, and humans confabulate too. The worst-case inevitability proofs he gestures at say nothing about real-task rates, and OpenAI's own paper frames hallucination as a fixable incentive problem. He is strongest here: AI error is confident, correlated at scale, and truth-indifferent, so unsupervised high-stakes use is genuinely disqualified. See the Reliability section for the full treatment.", "srcs": [["Why language models hallucinate (OpenAI, Sept 2025)", "https://openai.com/index/why-language-models-hallucinate/"], ["ChatGPT statistics: ~900M weekly users, ~25B ARR (2026)", "https://technologychecker.io/blog/chatgpt-statistics"], ["Why Language Models Hallucinate (OpenAI, 2025)", "https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.04664"], ["Hallucinations can be made statistically negligible (Suzuki et al.)", "https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.12187"]]}, {"id": "rot_economy", "label": "Rot economy / business idiots", "stakes": "S3", "scope": "political-economy", "count": 70, "instances": [{"date": "2023-11-20", "title": "Sam Altman, Freed", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-freed", "quote": "There will be some that see this as an opportunity to slow down — to build sustainably, profitable, and in a way that makes companies last for decades or centuries, and others that see Altman’s firing as a gun to the head of their growth-at-all-costs money machine."}, {"date": "2024-02-27", "title": "Software Has Eaten The Media", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-anti-economy", "quote": "Ultimately, the Rot Economy's core problem is that decisions are being made about the things you love that exist to satisfy a party — an algorithm, an executive, an investor — that has no real interest in the product itself."}, {"date": "2024-02-27", "title": "Software Has Eaten The Media", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-anti-economy", "quote": "In a logical tech economy, one would be terrified that so many bets have been made on such shaky ground, but we're in the Rot Economy, where an unsustainable product with few clear use cases can burn billions of dollars and fuel our climate crisis because the tech industry has run out of fucking ideas."}, {"date": "2024-03-11", "title": "Are We Watching The Internet Die?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/are-we-watching-the-internet-die", "quote": "This is, of course, the crux of Cory Doctorow's Enshittification theory, where Reddit has moved from pleasing users to pleasing its business customers to, now, pleasing shareholders at what will inevitably be the cost of the platform's quality."}, {"date": "2024-03-11", "title": "Are We Watching The Internet Die?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/are-we-watching-the-internet-die", "quote": "Generative AI might be steeped in the language of high fantasy, but it’s a tool, one that they will not admit is a terribly-flawed and unprofitable way to feed the growth-at-all-costs tech engine."}, {"date": "2024-04-15", "title": "They're Looting The Internet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-great-looting-of-the-internet", "quote": "As a result, these platforms were (and are) a form of bait-and-switch, the underpinning philosophy of Cory Doctorow's \"Enshittification\" theory, where platforms build massive monopolies based on offering good, useful services, and then slowly turn the screws on the customer to seek ever-growing profits."}, {"date": "2024-04-15", "title": "They're Looting The Internet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-great-looting-of-the-internet", "quote": "Yet as I've noted before, I feel that enshittification misses one crucial thing — that these companies aren't doing this out of a lack of profitability or failure of their business model, but because the modern internet has become somewhere between a social experiment and a human mining operation."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "Or, for that matter, whether ads would provide a perverse incentive for OpenAI to enshittify an already unreliable product."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "This is not big tech’s big plan to excuse building more data centers — it’s the death throes of twenty years of growth-at-all-costs thinking, because throwing a bunch of money at more servers and more engineers always seemed to create more growth."}, {"date": "2024-12-16", "title": "Never Forgive Them", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/never-forgive-them", "quote": "However, Cory’s theory lacks a real perpetrator beyond corporations that naturally say “alright we’re gonna do Enshittification now, watch this.” Where The Rot Economy separates is that growth is, in and of itself, the force that drives companies to enshittify."}, {"date": "2025-01-17", "title": "The Slop Society", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-slop-society", "quote": "That's because all roads lead back to the Rot Economy — the growth-at-all-costs mindset that means that the only thing that matters is growth of revenue, which comes from showing as many ads to you as possible."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "It uses less memory, fewer resources, and uses several quirky workarounds to adapt to the limited compute resources available — all things that you'd previously associate with Silicon Valley, except Silicon Valley's only interest, like the rest of the American tech industry, is The Rot Economy."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "It cares about growth at all costs, even if said costs were readily mitigable, or if the costs are ultimately self-defeating."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "The resentment boiling against this software is profound because the tech industry has become desperate and violative, showing such contempt for their customers that even Apple will force an inferior experience upon them to please the will of the Rot Economy and the growth-at-all-cost mindset of the markets."}, {"date": "2025-03-24", "title": "The Phony Comforts of AI Optimism", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/optimistic-cowardice", "quote": "My core theses — The Rot Economy (that the tech industry has become dominated by growth), The Rot-Com Bubble (that the tech industry has run out of hyper-growth ideas), and that generative AI has created a kind of capitalist death cult where nobody wants to admit that they're not making any money — are far from comfortable."}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "The Rot Economy has consumed the tech industry."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "The Business Idiot is the manager that doesn't seem to do anything but keeps being promoted, and the chief executive officer of a public company that says boring, specious nonsense about AI."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Artificial intelligence is the ultimate panacea for the Business Idiot — a tool that gives an impression of productivity with far more production than the Business Idiot themselves."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Because Benioff and Salesforce have got rich selling to fellow Business Idiots who then shove Salesforce into their organization without thinking about who would use it or how they'd use it other than in the most general ways."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Look at every single institution installing some sort of ChatGPT integration, and then look for the Business Idiot."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "In some ways, Sam Altman is the Business Idiot's antichrist, taking advantage of a society where the powerful rarely know much other than what they want to control or dominate."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "No, they don't, because the powerful are Business Idiots too, willing to accept anything that somebody brings along that makes them feel good, or bad in a way that they can make headlines with."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "In any case, Altman's whole Sloppenheimer motif has worked wonders on the Business Idiots in the markets and global governments that fear what artificial intelligence could do, even if they can't really define artificial intelligence, or what it could do, or what they're scared of."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "The fear of China's \"rise in AI\" is one partially based on sinophobia, and partially based on the fact that China has their own Business Idiots willing to shove hundreds of millions of dollars into data centers."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "A true Business Idiot never admits wrongdoing, and the more powerful the Business Idiot is, the more likely there are power structures that exist to avoid them having to do so."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "The media, captured by other Business Idiots, has become poisoned by power, deferring to its whims and ideals and treating CEOs with more respect, dignity and intelligence than anyone that works for them."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Yet none of this would be possible without the enabling layers, and those layers are teeming with both Business Idiots and those unfortunate enough to have learned from them."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Anyone who believes otherwise is a fucking moron — or, better put, just another Business Idiot."}, {"date": "2025-06-16", "title": "Sincerity Wins The War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sic", "quote": "As it stands, a reader — especially a Business Idiot — could be forgiven for thinking that OpenAI was now worth, or could be worth, over a trillion dollars, which is an egregious editorial failure."}, {"date": "2025-06-16", "title": "Sincerity Wins The War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sic", "quote": "News rarely feels like it appeals to the listener, reader or viewer, just an amorphous generalized “thing” of a person imagined in the mind of a Business Idiot."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "You can dress this up as \"growth stage\" or \"enshittification (it isn't by the way, generally price changes make things profitable, which this did not),\" but Cursor lied."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "My Rot-Com Bubble thesis suggests we're out of hypergrowth ideas, and yeah, I think we're out of ideas related to Large Language Models too."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "Back in February 2023, I wrote about The Rot Economy, and how everything in tech had become oriented around growth — even if it meant making products harder to use as a means of increasing user engagement or funnelling them toward more-profitable parts of an app."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "Back in June 2024, I wrote about the Rot-Com Bubble, and my greater theory that the tech industry has run out of hypergrowth ideas: In simple terms, big tech, Amazon, Google, Microsoft and Meta, but also a number of other companies, no longer has the “next big thing,” and jumped on AI out of an abundance of desperation."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Per Kyle Chayka of the New Yorker, “Facebook’s feed, now choked with A.I.-generated garbage and short-form videos, is well into the third act of enshittification.” The third stage is critical, in that it’s when the company also turns on its business customers."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "What if all of this was utterly senseless?* As I wrote last year, the tech industry has run out of hypergrowth ideas, facing something I call “the Rot Com bubble.” In simple terms, they’re only “doing AI” because there do not appear to be any other viable ideas to continue the Rot Economy’s eternal growth-at-all-costs dance."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Every single person who has asked this has been poorly-read — both in terms of my work and the surrounding economics and technological possibilities of Large Language Models — and believes they’re defending technology, when in reality they’re defending growth, and the Rot Economy’s growth-at-all-costs mindset."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "The enshittification of the shareholder has the downstream effect of an enshittification of the media and Wall Street analysts writ large."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "It is a global event where we’ve realized how the global elite are just as stupid and ignorant as anybody you’d meet on the street — Business Idiots that couldn’t think their way out of a paper bag, empowered by other Business Idiots that desperately need to believe that everything will grow forever."}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "The Era of the Business Idiot, probably my favourite piece I wrote this year, the story of how middle management has seized power, breeding out true meritocracy and value-creation in favor of symbolic growth and superficial intelligence."}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis, a piece about The Enshittifinancial Crisis, the fourth stage of enshittification, where companies turn on their shareholders."}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "A panel in Seattle with Cory Doctorow about Enshittification and The Rot Economy."}, {"date": "2026-05-06", "title": "Am I Meant To Be Impressed?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/am-i-meant-to-be-impressed", "quote": "The only reason Google, Amazon and Microsoft are being tolerated at their current excess is because their non-AI segments continue to grow through endless price-increases and enshittification, and its external business units — by which I mean OpenAI and Anthropic — are yet to die."}, {"date": "2026-05-19", "title": "AI Is Too Expensive", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-too-expensive", "quote": "It’s hard to tell if this is AI psychosis or just classic Business Idiot bullshit."}, {"date": "2026-05-19", "title": "AI Is Too Expensive", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-too-expensive", "quote": "Yet even a Business Idiot eventually realizes that too much money is being spent, and the first one of these dimwits to cut their token budget will send the rest of them running for the doors."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "AI is a perfect storm of failed concepts and organizations, and the apex of the Era of the Business Idiot, an epoch where we’re ruled by people so thoroughly disconnected from the actual workforce that it was inevitable that a technology would be created specifically to grift them."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "And that’s why Business Idiots love it."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "A Business Idiot, given his druthers, can sit there and fuck around and make an LLM spit out something that makes him feel like he’s coding, which in turn makes him feel that you, a lazy and stupid engineer, could do even more with the power of AI."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "You laugh, but this is genuinely how the majority of managers and executives think and act, and now they have a special chatbot that can fart out functional-enough prototypes to convince a Business Idiot they can do anything, because executives and managers do not regularly do much work."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "They’re Business Idiots, and they are your enemy."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Even those who believe they’re aligned with the Business Idiots by supporting and using Large Language Models are the enemy, because The Business Idiots believe that “AI” will simply remove anybody else from the picture, automating work, creativity, communication, friendship, and that includes anyone that helped its ascent."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "And yet none of it’s really working, because Business Idiots don’t really know how anything works. LLMs Are Built To Coddle Losers As I said back in the original piece, think of The Business Idiot as a kind of con artist, except the con has become the standard way of doing business for an alarmingly large part of society."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Thankfully, The Business Idiots have captured both the media and the markets, twisting the definition of a “good company” into one measured by these very same questions."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Boz, like every other Business Idiot, exists to extract value from others and get rewarded by shareholders."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "When somebody badmouths AI, the Business Idiot must defend it with everything they have, because attacking LLMs is attacking the output of an LLM, which is in turn a judgment on those who are tolerant of its mediocrity and impossible-to-avoid hallucinations."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "You see, if you demand good work with intention, that might mean the Business Idiot actually had to do something, and that’s not what The Business Idiot signed up for."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Business Idiots did well to pressure modern journalism into conflating scrutiny with a lack of curiosity. To ask too many questions is “unfair.” To not immediately assume that LLMs are getting “exponentially better” is to be an ignorant luddite."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "That ignorance is a sign of laziness, and of the dominance of the Business Idiot mindset."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "He’s doing it because he, like every Business Idiot, has no idea what to do other than spend money, hire people, or fire people."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "That “demand” is not an extrapolation of demand for AI services, but for debt’s hunger to invest in something private credit and banks believe in. - Private credit and banks believe in data centers based on flawed maths and magical thinking, because they too are run by Business Idiots."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Like every greedy dullard, Business Idiots backing data centers are easily won over by the blatant lie that a data center is an “AI factory,” conjuring up images of large buildings that print money with little human labor needed."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "These Business Idiots are too informed by other Business Idiots, like the sell-side and buy-side analysts that have no interest in talking about what might happen in the distant future when they can conjure up plausible-sounding statements that pump their bags."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "And because these hyperscalers were so aggressive with their buildouts, the Business Idiots conflated that hunger with some sort of proof of massive demand for AI."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "I believe that neither OpenAI nor Anthropic have a future, and that their revenues are only made possible through venture subsidies for startups using their models and the experimental revenue of Business Idiots that don’t really know why they’re “doing AI” in the first place."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "I write this newsletter to hopefully do three things: - First, to tell you that the Business Idiot class wants you to doubt yourself, because whether you recognize it or not, they’re engaged in acts of information warfare against you."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "The computer has done many wonderful things for me, despite what all the Business Idiots say."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "The media and markets are informed by people that neither understand technology nor history, and Business Idiots that have reached the heights of their careers through diplomacy and ratfucking that care only about attention and adulation for things that other people do."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "The only reason that we’ve been “doing AI” with such ferocity and veracity is that most companies are beholden to Business Idiots disconnected from production who have no real understanding of their underlying firms’ outputs, and thus have very little way of measuring them."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "Every day I hear from someone who is dealing with the wrath of a different Business Idiot who doesn't do anything other than demand more deliverables in a smaller timeframe with less people because you keep laying people off. If you are a worker at a tech company, I fucking see you. I feel your pain."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "So many of you truly love making good software and want to do good things in the world and feel impeded by the Business Idiots and mocked by the boosters who seem to care more about your bosses than anything to do with software or innovation."}], "verdict": "Partly right on the diagnosis, weak on the mechanism", "analysis": "He correctly senses structural dysfunction and degraded products, and is a vivid popularizer. But 'rot economy' is a symptom-label, not a mechanism. The rigorous accounts locate cause in institutions: <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_rot_economy__c1\" data-tip=\"cat_rot_economy__c1\" href=\"https://www.ineteconomics.org/research/research-papers/profits-without-prosperity-how-stock-buybacks-manipulate-the-market-and-leave-most-americans-worse-off\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">buybacks (Lazonick)</a>, shareholder primacy and financialization (Konczal), <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_rot_economy__c3\" data-tip=\"cat_rot_economy__c3\" href=\"https://www.nber.org/papers/w23396\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">concentration and labor share (Autor)</a>, and the direction of technology (<a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_rot_economy__c2\" data-tip=\"cat_rot_economy__c2\" href=\"https://www.wheresyoured.at/rot-economics-an-interview-with-mits-daron-acemoglu\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Acemoglu, whom he interviewed, who calls it choice not exhaustion</a>). Right that it is broken, fuzzy on why.", "srcs": [["Profits Without Prosperity (Lazonick, HBR 2014)", "https://hbr.org/2014/09/profits-without-prosperity"], ["Rot Economics, interview with Daron Acemoglu (Zitron, 2024)", "https://www.wheresyoured.at/rot-economics-an-interview-with-mits-daron-acemoglu"]]}, {"id": "not_cheaper", "label": "Not getting cheaper / costs only rise", "stakes": "S1", "scope": "industry-economics", "count": 50, "instances": [{"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "Or, put another way, each additional step becomes increasingly (and exponentially) more expensive to take."}, {"date": "2024-07-08", "title": "Pop Culture", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/pop-culture", "quote": "Generative AI costs far too much, isn't getting cheaper, uses too much power, and doesn't do enough to justify its existence."}, {"date": "2024-07-24", "title": "Rot Economics - An Interview With MIT's Daron Acemoglu", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/rot-economics-an-interview-with-mits-daron-acemoglu", "quote": "So the thing is — and I understand why you're making these assumptions — what if it doesn't get cheaper?"}, {"date": "2024-07-29", "title": "How Does OpenAI Survive?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/to-serve-altman", "quote": "OpenAI's costs have only increased over time, and the cost of making these models \"better\" are only increasing, and have yet to, to paraphrase Goldman Sachs' Jim Covello, solve the kind of complex problems that would justify their cost."}, {"date": "2024-07-29", "title": "How Does OpenAI Survive?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/to-serve-altman", "quote": "If it hasn't, it likely will be required to buy tens of thousands — if not millions — of hours of footage, which will be multitudes more expensive than the $250 million it paid to News Corp to train on its articles."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "Doing so will only cause more problems — there isn’t a chance in hell that Sora is profitable, and I’m fairly sure it’s even more expensive to run than ChatGPT, and I imagine its visual inconsistencies and hallucinations would make for some entertaining content for YouTubers and tech reporters."}, {"date": "2024-09-16", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/subprimeai", "quote": "More powerful\" never seems to mean \"does more,\" and \"more powerful\" oftentimes means \"more expensive,\" meaning that you've just made something that doesn't do more but does cost more to run."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "It's also going to be much, much more expensive to run, as the \"chain-of-thought\" \"reasoning\" that it does requires a bunch of extra calculations (an indeterminate amount that OpenAI is deliberately hiding), and OpenAI can't even seem to come up with a meaningful use case."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "The Information also estimated back in July that OpenAI's training costs would balloon to $3 billion in 2024, and it’s fair to assume that models like o1 and GPT-5 (also known as “Orion”) will be significantly more expensive to train."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "The constant refrain I hear from VCs and AI fantasists is that \"chips will bring down the cost of inference,\" yet I don't see any proof of that happening, nor do I think it'll happen quickly enough for these companies to turn things around."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "Its products do not scale like traditional software, in that the more users it gets, the more expensive its services are to run because its models are so compute-intensive."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "Worse still, OpenAI has, while delaying its next model (GPT-5), promised to launch its o3 reasoning model after saying it wouldn't do so, which is strange, because it turns out that o3 is actually way more expensive to run than people thought."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "Reasoning models are almost always more expensive to operate, as they involve the model “checking” its work, which, in turn, requires more calculations and more computation."}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "DeepSeek is not OpenAI, and OpenAI’s latest models only get more expensive as time drags on."}, {"date": "2025-06-30", "title": "Make Fun Of Them", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/make-fun-of-them", "quote": "The cost of inference is coming down?"}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "The cost of tokens going down is not the same thing as the cost of inference goes down!"}, {"date": "2025-08-06", "title": "AI Is A Money Trap", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-a-money-trap", "quote": "The net result of these cost increases means that Cursor’s product is less attractive to its customers, and will thus make it less money."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "BOOSTER QUIP: Umm, five really smart guys got together and wrote AI 2027, which is a very real-sounding extrapolation that- - ULTIMATE BOOSTER QUIP: The Cost Of Inference Is Coming Down!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "The Cost Of Inference Has Gone Up Over Time!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "The Cost Of Inference Went Up Because The Models Are Now Built To Burn More Tokens - Could The Cost Of Inference Go Down?"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "If you say AI companies burn billions, they’ll say the cost of inference is coming down."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "ULTIMATE BOOSTER QUIP: The Cost Of Inference Is Coming Down!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "The \"cost of inference\" conversation comes from articles like this that say that we now have models that are cheaper that can now hit higher benchmark scores, though this article is from November 2024, and the comparison it makes is between GPT-3 (November 2021) and Llama 3.2 3B (September 2024)."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "The suggestion, in any case, is that \"the cost of inference is going down 10x year-over-year.\" The problem, however, is that these are raw token costs, not actual expressions or evaluations of token burn in a practical setting. Worse still… Well, the cost of inference actually went up."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "These tokens are also more expensive."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "The Cost Of Inference Has Gone Up"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Could The Cost Of Inference Go Down? ...maybe?"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "While open-source models typically cost less per token to run, the study suggests this advantage can be “easily offset if they require more tokens to reason about a given problem.” And models keep getting bigger and more expensive, too."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "In my opinion — and this is just my gut instinct — I believe that it is either significantly more expensive to run Anthropic than we know, or Anthropic’s leaked (and stated) revenue numbers are worse than we believe."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "Costs increased by $59.1 million, primarily across compute categories, but with a large ($2 million since January) increase in monthly costs for S3 storage."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "As I’ll get to later in the piece, Cursor’s costs exploded from $6.19 million in May 2025 to $12.67 million in June 2025, and I believe this is a direct result of Anthropic’s sudden and aggressive cost increases."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "Anthropic’s AWS Costs Increase Linearly With Revenue, Consuming The Majority Of Each Dollar Anthropic Makes - As A Reminder, It Also Spends Hundreds Of Millions Or Billions On Google Cloud Too So, I wanted to visualize this part of the story, because I think it’s important to see the various different scenarios."}, {"date": "2025-10-20", "title": "This Is How Much Anthropic and Cursor Spend On Amazon Web Services", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/costs", "quote": "The cost of inference is clearly increasing for customers, but based on its escalating monthly costs, the cost of inference appears to be high for Anthropic too, though it’s impossible to tell how much of its compute is based on training versus running inference."}, {"date": "2025-11-12", "title": "Exclusive: Here's How Much OpenAI Spends On Inference and Its Revenue Share With Microsoft", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai_docs", "quote": "OpenAI’s inference costs have risen consistently over the last 18 months, too."}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "Large Language Models are limited, AI agents are a pipedream and simply do not work, AI-powered products are unreliable and coding LLMs make developers slower, and the cost of inference — the way in which a model produces its output — keeps going up."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Everything is more expensive, and every tech product has gotten worse, all so that every company can “do AI,” whatever the fuck that means."}, {"date": "2026-03-10", "title": "The Beginning Of History", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-beginning-of-history", "quote": "Iran changes that in the most obvious way possible — if prices soar, interest rates may follow, and if rates go up, even by a point or two of a percentage, financing the tens and hundreds of billions of dollars in borrowing that the AI bubble demands will become significantly more expensive."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "This pairs badly with the fact that the Japanese government is considering interest rate hikes thanks to the continuing chaos in the Middle East, which will make debt more expensive."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "As AI labs grow, their costs increase dramatically, both in their immediate compute costs and the demands from GPU providers for up-front cash to secure future compute allocation."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "AI labs are thus forced to raise prices on AI startups, either through tolls (priority processing) or raw cost increases."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "Another important detail: one of the ways that AI labs raise prices isn’t even through “making things more expensive,” but selling access to models that burn more tokens. Think of this as the variable rate mortgage of the Subprime AI Crisis."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "I’m gonna be honest I just don’t give a shit about Mythos or Capybara or any blatant leaks intended to spook cybersecurity stocks, especially as these models are also meant to be much more compute-intensive, and thus, vastly more expensive to run."}, {"date": "2026-03-31", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis Is Here", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-subprime-ai-crisis-is-here", "quote": "And the magical part about Large Language Models is that your most engaged customers are also your most-expensive, and the more-intensive the work, the more expensive the outputs become."}, {"date": "2026-04-08", "title": "AI Is Really Weird", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-really-weird", "quote": "Chatbot connected to a knowledge base, like we’ve had for years but worse and more expensive."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "Every day the news reminds you that everything sucks and is more expensive unless you’re in AI, where you’ll be given as much money and told you’re the most special person alive."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "They also assumed, I imagine, that the cost of tokens would come down over time, versus what actually happened — while prices for some models might have come down, newer “reasoning” models burn way more tokens, which means the cost of inference has, somehow, gotten higher over time."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "Generative AI subscriptions are like if Uber charged users $20 a month for 100 rides of any distance under 100 miles, and if gas was $150 a gallon, and Uber paid for the gas because somebody insisted that oil would one day be too cheap to meter."}, {"date": "2026-05-21", "title": "Anthropic's \"Profitability\" Swindle", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/anthropics-profitability-swindle", "quote": "Costs increase linearly with revenue, and will continue to do so in perpetuity."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "Four years and a trillion dollars in, AI is more expensive, its companies more cash-intensive, its products just as unreliable, and its boosters more desperate than ever to make you ignore reality as a means of empowering one of a few ultra-rich oafs."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "I must repeat myself: AI is more expensive today than it was three years ago, and it is not getting cheaper. Sam Altman’s comments about “intelligence too cheap to meter” were lies."}], "verdict": "Mostly wrong on the metric that matters", "analysis": "Wrong on the most important measure, defensible only at the edges. Price per unit of capability collapsed. <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_not_cheaper__c1\" data-tip=\"cat_not_cheaper__c1\" href=\"https://epoch.ai/data-insights/llm-inference-price-trends\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Epoch AI finds the price for a fixed benchmark score fell roughly 50x to 200x per year</a>, <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_not_cheaper__c2\" data-tip=\"cat_not_cheaper__c2\" href=\"https://a16z.com/llmflation-llm-inference-cost/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">a16z pegs it near 10x per year</a>, and <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_not_cheaper__c3\" data-tip=\"cat_not_cheaper__c3\" href=\"https://www.theargumentmag.com/p/ais-biggest-critic-has-lost-the-plot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GPT-4-level intelligence is about one-thousandth its launch cost</a>. So 'not getting cheaper' and 'too cheap to meter was a lie' are false for price-per-capability and price-per-token. His point survives only narrowly: <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_not_cheaper__c4\" data-tip=\"cat_not_cheaper__c4\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GPT-4.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the top frontier model at launch can cost more (GPT-4.5 at $75/$150)</a>, and <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_not_cheaper__c5\" data-tip=\"cat_not_cheaper__c5\" href=\"https://www.codeant.ai/blogs/input-vs-output-vs-reasoning-tokens-cost\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">reasoning models burn about 10x the tokens</a>, so cost-per-task and a lab's total spend can rise even as unit prices crater. He treats the exceptions as if they refute the rule.", "srcs": [["LLM inference prices have fallen rapidly (Epoch AI)", "https://epoch.ai/data-insights/llm-inference-price-trends"], ["LLMflation: inference cost falling ~10x/year (a16z)", "https://a16z.com/llmflation-llm-inference-cost/"], ["AI's biggest critic has lost the plot (Kelsey Piper)", "https://www.theargumentmag.com/p/ais-biggest-critic-has-lost-the-plot"]]}, {"id": "useless", "label": "Useless / no real value", "stakes": "S1", "scope": "tech-viability", "count": 46, "instances": [{"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "The amount of data it needs is several multitudes more than currently exists at a time when algorithms are happily-promoting and encouraging AI-generated slop, and thousands of human journalists have lost their jobs, with others being forced to create generic search-engine-optimized slop."}, {"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "As generative AI does not \"know\" anything, when fed reams of content generated by other models, they begin learning rules based on content generated by a machine guessing at what it should be writing rather than communicating meaning, making it somewhere between useless and actively harmful as training data."}, {"date": "2024-05-13", "title": "Expectations Versus Reality", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/expectations-versus-reality", "quote": "The answer, it turns out, is “not very well.” In a piece for FXGuide, Mike Seymour sat down with Shy Kids, the people behind Air Head, and revealed how Sora is, in many ways, totally useless for making films."}, {"date": "2024-06-11", "title": "Silicon Valley's False Prophet", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/false-prophet", "quote": "While ChatGPT isn’t inherently useless, Altman realizes that it’s impossible to generate the kind of funding and hype he needs based on its actual achievements, and that to continue to accumulate power and money, he must speciously hype it to wealthy and powerful people who don’t participate in the creation of anything."}, {"date": "2024-07-16", "title": "Put Up Or Shut Up", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/put-up-or-shut-up", "quote": "The media seems nigh-on incapable of accepting that generative AI is a big, stupid, costly and environmentally-destructive bubble, to the point that they'll happily accept marketing slop and vague platitudes about how big something that's already here will be in the future based on a remarkable lack of proof."}, {"date": "2024-07-29", "title": "How Does OpenAI Survive?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/to-serve-altman", "quote": "To be clear, I am not saying generative AI is completely useless, or that it hasn't got any product-market fit."}, {"date": "2024-08-05", "title": "Burst Damage", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/burst-damage", "quote": "And a lack of creativity in the tallest towers of Silicon Valley and Redmond has allowed the richest men in the industry to be conned by a snake oil machine that loses billions of dollars."}, {"date": "2024-09-26", "title": "The Other Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/saaspocalypse-now", "quote": "Scenario 1 is obviously dangerous, offering a tool that costs a great deal of money to provide only a little value to customers for free, meaning that at best you'll have customers that lose you money every single time they interact with the product."}, {"date": "2024-09-26", "title": "The Other Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/saaspocalypse-now", "quote": "As a result, generative AI kind of felt like the perfect SaaS snake oil, a magical new way to indefinitely charge customers for the thing that they already should have."}, {"date": "2024-11-13", "title": "Lost In The Future", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/lost-in-the-future", "quote": "Our social networks are so algorithmically charged that they barely show us the things we want them to anymore, with executives dedicated to filling our feeds with AI-generated slop because despite being the customer, we are also the revenue mechanism."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "The tech industry is over-leveraged, having doubled, tripled, quadrupled down on generative AI — a technology that doesn't do much more than it did a few months ago and won't do much more than it can do now."}, {"date": "2024-12-16", "title": "Never Forgive Them", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/never-forgive-them", "quote": "Tim Cook is a wolf in sheep’s clothing, slowly allowing the rot to seep into Apple’s products, slowly adding bothersome subscription products and useless AI features to chip away at the user experience."}, {"date": "2025-01-17", "title": "The Slop Society", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-slop-society", "quote": "Facebook is crammed with fake accounts, AI-generated slop, and nonsense groups teeming with boomers posting that they \"wish we'd return to a culture of respect\" as they're recommended their third racist meme of the day."}, {"date": "2025-01-17", "title": "The Slop Society", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-slop-society", "quote": "Meta has fired the starting gun of the Slop Society."}, {"date": "2025-01-17", "title": "The Slop Society", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-slop-society", "quote": "Meta will push as much AI slop as it wants, both created by its generative models and their users, and massively ramp up content that riles up users with little regard for the consequences."}, {"date": "2025-02-17", "title": "The Generative AI Con", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/longcon", "quote": "Deep Research repeatedly citing SEO-bait as a primary source proves that these models, even when grinding their gears as hard as humanely possible, are exceedingly mediocre, deeply untrustworthy, and ultimately useless."}, {"date": "2025-02-17", "title": "The Generative AI Con", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/longcon", "quote": "Deep Research is the AI slop of academia — low-quality research-slop built for people that don't really care about quality or substance, and it’s not immediately obvious who it’s for."}, {"date": "2025-02-17", "title": "The Generative AI Con", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/longcon", "quote": "When will the media stop treating every single expensive, stupid, irksome, quasi-useless new product is magical, and start asking these people to show us the fucking future already?"}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "As a product, Operator barely works."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "Anthropic, much like OpenAI, has categorically failed to productize its Large Language Model, with the only product it appears to have pushed being Computer Use, a similarly-useless AI model that can sometimes successfully do in minutes what it takes you to do in seconds using a web browser."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "It doesn’t make humans better, it reduces their work to a stagnant, unremarkable slop in every way it can, and reduces the cognition of those who come to rely on it, and it costs hundreds of billions of dollars and a return to fossil fuels for some reason."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "Worse still, investors and the media have run cover for the fact that these models don't really do much more than they did a year ago and for the overall diminishing returns of Large Language Models."}, {"date": "2025-04-28", "title": "Reality Check", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/reality-check", "quote": "Check out this quote: So you're saying this ***experimental software launched to an indeterminate amount of people that barely works is going to make OpenAI $13 billion in 2025, and $29 billion in 2026, and later down the line $125 billion in 2029?"}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Why would companies push generative AI in seemingly every part of their service, even though customers don't like it and it doesn't really work?"}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "We’re not just drowning in a sea of slop — we’re in a constant state of corporate AI beta tests, new “features” sprouting out of our products like new limbs that sometimes function normally but often attempt to strangle us."}, {"date": "2025-06-16", "title": "Sincerity Wins The War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sic", "quote": "Companies can raise their prices specifically to raise their profits, Meta can literally not make a metaverse, AI can do very little to actually automate your real job, and the media will still tell you to shut the fuck up and eat their truth-slop."}, {"date": "2025-06-30", "title": "Make Fun Of Them", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/make-fun-of-them", "quote": "Is it because it feels icky to interrupt Satya Nadella as he waffles on about using Copilot all the time by saying “hey man, Microsoft Teams is broken, tons of people feel this way, why?” or “why have you let MSN.com turn into a hub of AI slop and outright disinformation?” Oh no!"}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "If you say there are no real use cases, they’ll say that ChatGPT has 700 million weekly users."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "These reports are slop."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "By comparison, AI boosters are the first to get TV appearances and offers to be on panels, their coverage featured prominently on Techmeme, selling slop-like books called shit like The Future Of Intelligence: Masters Of The Brain featuring 18 interviews with different CEOs that all say the same thing."}, {"date": "2025-12-31", "title": "2025, A Retrospective", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/2025-a-retrospective", "quote": "Make Fun Of Them, the piece that restarted my fire after a bit of a low point, where I call for a radical new approach to tech CEOs: mocking them, because they talk like idiots and provide little value to society outside of their dedication to shareholder value."}, {"date": "2026-02-26", "title": "On NVIDIA and Analyslop", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/on-nvidia-and-analyslop", "quote": "This week, alleged financial analyst Citrini Research (not to be confused with Andrew Left’s Citron Research) put out a truly awful piece called the “2028 Global Intelligence Crisis,” slop-filled scare-fiction written and framed with the authority of deeply-founded analysis, so much so that it caused a global selloff in stocks."}, {"date": "2026-03-24", "title": "The AI Industry Is Lying To You", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-industry-is-lying-to-you", "quote": "Anybody who actually works knows that the most productive-seeming people are often also the most-useless, as they’re doing things to seem productive rather than producing anything of note."}, {"date": "2026-03-24", "title": "The AI Industry Is Lying To You", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-industry-is-lying-to-you", "quote": "They were pressured by Amazon to take up useless skills and build useless things in an expensive and inefficient way, and ended up losing their job despite taking up tools they didn’t like under duress."}, {"date": "2026-03-24", "title": "The AI Industry Is Lying To You", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-industry-is-lying-to-you", "quote": "AI’s supposed ability to “write all code” really means that every major software company is filling their codebases with slop while massively increasing their operating expenses."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "Soulless LinkedIn slop makes you feel frustration with a person for their lack of authenticity, but you can still imagine how they forced it out of their heads."}, {"date": "2026-04-14", "title": "I Will Never Respect A Website", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/i-will-never-respect-a-website", "quote": "A Scenario Illustrating How Anthropic Fucks Over Its Customers It’s January 14 2026, and you just read The Atlantic’s breathless hype-slop about Claude Code, believing that it was “bigger than the ChatGPT moment,” that it was an “inflection point for AI progress,” and that it could build whatever software you imagined."}, {"date": "2026-05-06", "title": "Am I Meant To Be Impressed?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/am-i-meant-to-be-impressed", "quote": "Google Won’t Talk About Its AI Revenues, But Anthropic’s Spend Likely Accounts For Most Of Google Cloud’s Growth God, everyone loves to slurp down Sundar’s slop."}, {"date": "2026-05-19", "title": "AI Is Too Expensive", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-too-expensive", "quote": "In some cases, the pressure to use AI for everything is turning companies’ software stacks into slop."}, {"date": "2026-05-19", "title": "AI Is Too Expensive", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-too-expensive", "quote": "Something about LLMs has done something to its technical leadership, something that makes them talk strange and send weird slide decks with confusing, slop-ridden sentences."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "As he said in 2018, to Boz, “all the work \\[Meta does\\] in growth is justified.” That includes deliberately making notifications less useful, injecting clickbait and AI slop into your feed, and hiding chronological feeds behind an Escher painting of different menu options."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "Law schools would collapse, because legal internships would become useless and law firms would no longer have need for the thousands of new associates, because ChatGPT could just draft it all."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "We’d be able to point to companies that adopted AI and then completely fucking exploded. We’d be able to point to useless coworkers who were now doing impressive, meaningful work."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "When some of you are pushed to prove the ROI of AI, you immediately return to boring talking points about Uber, or the Dot Com Bubble, or some other slop fed to you by people actively conning you at this very moment. I mean this with as much empathy as I can muster: if you’re a huge AI booster, why do you defend this so vociferously?"}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "These multi-millionaire midwits have been “doing AI” because everybody else is doing it, burning millions of dollars to turn their code into slop (see: Zillow) or have their engineers compete to see who can spend the most money (see: Meta and multiple other companies)."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "While we’ve discovered the shovelware, that’s all that LLMs have given us — “more” apps, with the vast majority being useless, insecure slopware."}], "verdict": "Mostly wrong, and a refusal to update", "analysis": "His most self-damaging claim, and it has aged worse each year. 'Useless, no value, snake oil' is contradicted by <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_useless__c1\" data-tip=\"cat_useless__c1\" href=\"https://technologychecker.io/blog/chatgpt-statistics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">about 900M weekly users</a>, <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_useless__c2\" data-tip=\"cat_useless__c2\" href=\"https://www.nber.org/papers/w31161\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">a real support-agent productivity experiment</a>, and <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_useless__c3\" data-tip=\"cat_useless__c3\" href=\"https://www.digitalapplied.com/blog/ai-coding-adoption-statistics-2026-50-data-points\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the agentic coding shift that engineers actually adopted</a>. <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_useless__c4\" data-tip=\"cat_useless__c4\" href=\"https://www.theargumentmag.com/p/ais-biggest-critic-has-lost-the-plot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">He hedges when pressed and in 2026 even denies he ever said it, a motte-and-bailey.</a> Repeating 'useless' four years after the tools shipped is less a claim than a refusal to update. The defensible version, that enterprise ROI is unproven, is a different and narrower claim.", "srcs": [["Generative AI at Work, support-agent RCT (Brynjolfsson, Li, Raymond)", "https://www.nber.org/papers/w31161"], ["ChatGPT statistics: ~900M weekly users, ~25B ARR (2026)", "https://technologychecker.io/blog/chatgpt-statistics"], ["AI's biggest critic has lost the plot (Kelsey Piper, The Argument)", "https://www.theargumentmag.com/p/ais-biggest-critic-has-lost-the-plot"]]}, {"id": "no_roi", "label": "No ROI / returns can't be shown", "stakes": "S2", "scope": "industry-economics", "count": 22, "instances": [{"date": "2024-09-16", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/subprimeai", "quote": "The markets are extremely skeptical of the generative AI boom, and NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang had no real answers about AI's return on investment, leading to an historic $279 billion drop in NVIDIA's market cap in a single day."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "I’m not even saying that there’s no returns, or that LLMs don’t do anything, or even that there’s no possible commercial use for generative AI."}, {"date": "2025-05-21", "title": "The Era Of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-era-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "There are slot machines with a better ROI than this shit."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "A neocloud is a specialist cloud compute company that exists only to provide access to GPUs for AI, unlike Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud, all of which have healthy businesses selling other kinds of compute, with AI (as I’ll get into later) failing to provide much of a return on investment."}, {"date": "2026-02-26", "title": "On NVIDIA and Analyslop", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/on-nvidia-and-analyslop", "quote": "The majority of CEOs report little or no return on investment from AI, with a study of 6000 CEOs across the US, UK, Germany and Australia finding that “more than 80% \\[detected\\] no discernable impact from AI on either employment or productivity.” Nevertheless, you read “GPU” and “North Dakota” and you think “wow!"}, {"date": "2026-03-17", "title": "Why Are We Still Doing This?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/why-are-we-still-doing-this", "quote": "Really though, where is the ROI? Who is actually getting a profit out of this?"}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "There has never been — and never will be — an economically-feasible way to offer services powered by LLMs without charging the actual token burn of each user, and in the process of deceiving said users, these companies have created products with illusory benefits and questionable return on investment."}, {"date": "2026-04-28", "title": "AI's Economics Don't Make Sense", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ais-economics-dont-make-sense", "quote": "I’m not sure any business investing these vast amounts of money in tokens is seeing any return on investment, which is why every study about AI’s ROI struggles to find much evidence that it exists."}, {"date": "2026-05-19", "title": "AI Is Too Expensive", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-too-expensive", "quote": "How the fuck do you actually measure the return on investment for that spend? How many tokens does it take to do one thing?"}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "As I’ve discussed previously, nobody really knows how to measure the ROI of AI, and the naturally-chaotic nature of LLMs makes it impossible to measure how much it might even cost: Marc Benioff isn’t spending $300 million a year on Anthropic tokens because it’s doing something."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Seriously, somebody please show me a company spending millions of dollars on AI tokens that can also express a clear, indisputable return on investment. Show me the actual returns."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "That’s because, as I’ve said before, nobody can actually measure the ROI of AI, or even create a standard measurement of the cost of a task thanks to the inevitable hallucination-prone nature of LLMs and the ever-growing list of different harnesses and “agentic” (sigh) interfaces."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "If you can’t measure how good something is, how much it might cost, or what your return on investment might be, it’s fair to ask why you’re even paying for it in the first place."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "People are (reasonably!) harping on about the ROI problem, but I think the “can’t really measure the cost” part is an even bigger problem."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "We wouldn’t have to talk about the fucking potential at all because we’d be able to point to what was going on because it would be obvious! Whenever Someone Tries To Measure AI’s ROI They Have To Admit It Doesn’t Exist Last week, Bain & Co."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "released a study of 951 executives from companies with more than $100 million in revenue, and unsurprisingly, the data did not declaratively explain what the ROI of AI was: 10% of…what?"}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "LLM Users Are The Victims Of A Con If AI had ROI, we’d be able to point with specificity to inarguable examples of economic impacts. AI boosters can jerk their binguses all they like about how Spotify’s CEO said its best engineers don’t write any code anymore."}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "When some of you are pushed to prove the ROI of AI, you immediately return to boring talking points about Uber, or the Dot Com Bubble, or some other slop fed to you by people actively conning you at this very moment. I mean this with as much empathy as I can muster: if you’re a huge AI booster, why do you defend this so vociferously?"}, {"date": "2026-06-02", "title": "AI Doesn't Have ROI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-doesnt-have-roi", "quote": "And yet with all the money, all the attention, all the resources, all the land, all the power, all the affordances and excuses and endless fucking applause for mediocrity, nobody can actually point to the ROI of AI, because it doesn’t exist outside of it burping out stolen content and enriching and ingratiating billionaire dullards."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "I sure hope that’s happe-OH MY GOD! As I discussed last week, you can’t measure the cost of a particular task with AI, nor can you measure its return on investment."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "Its services cost too much to run, its progenitors have no path to profitability, and no amount of rigged benchmarks and anecdotal examples of theoretical engineering teams that are “10x’d” can make up for the fact that you can’t measure the cost of an LLM-driven task or its return on investment."}, {"date": "2026-06-08", "title": "AI Is Slowing Down", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/ai-is-slowing-down", "quote": "Anyone claiming that you have to “measure AI’s ROI differently” is attempting to con either you or themselves."}], "verdict": "Mostly correct, his sharpest distinctive claim", "analysis": "Where he is most credible. <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_no_roi__c1\" data-tip=\"cat_no_roi__c1\" href=\"https://fortune.com/2025/08/18/mit-report-95-percent-generative-ai-pilots-at-companies-failing-cfo/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The MIT/NANDA 2025 report found about 95 percent of enterprise gen-AI pilots produced no P&L impact</a>, <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_no_roi__c2\" data-tip=\"cat_no_roi__c2\" href=\"https://www.banandre.com/blog/mckinsey-2025-ai-report-widespread-adoption-limited-impact\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">McKinsey found most firms see no enterprise-level EBIT effect</a>, and <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_no_roi__c3\" data-tip=\"cat_no_roi__c3\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/06/05/the-token-bill-comes-due-inside-the-industry-scramble-to-manage-ais-runaway-costs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">companies from Uber to Brex imposed hard token caps citing unclear returns</a>. 'Enterprise ROI is largely unproven at current prices' is well-supported. It weakens only when he slides from 'unproven ROI' to 'no value.'", "srcs": [["MIT/NANDA: 95% of enterprise gen-AI pilots show no P&L impact (2025)", "https://nanda.media.mit.edu/"], ["The token bill comes due: enterprises scramble on AI costs (TechCrunch)", "https://techcrunch.com/2026/06/05/the-token-bill-comes-due-inside-the-industry-scramble-to-manage-ais-runaway-costs/"]]}, {"id": "hit_wall", "label": "Hit a wall / no improvement", "stakes": "S1", "scope": "tech-viability", "count": 13, "instances": [{"date": "2024-04-04", "title": "Bubble Trouble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/bubble-trouble", "quote": "According to data from data.ai (formerly known as AppAnnie), ChatGPT's downloads have also begun to drop from a high of just over 700,000 a week to a plateau around 450,000 to 500,000 a week since early 2023."}, {"date": "2024-07-29", "title": "How Does OpenAI Survive?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/to-serve-altman", "quote": "While the US steadily added new electricity generation capacity in the second half of the 1900s, things started to plateau in the 2010s."}, {"date": "2024-09-16", "title": "The Subprime AI Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/subprimeai", "quote": "Putting aside terms like \"performance\" — as they are largely used as a means of generating things \"accurately\" or \"faster\" rather than being good at stuff — Large Language Models have effectively plateaued."}, {"date": "2024-10-02", "title": "OpenAI Is A Bad Business", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business", "quote": "Compare that to the story from the New York Times, which suggested that OpenAI is still only on course to make one billion dollars from selling access to its own models — which highly suggests that growth has plateaued for its cloud services, and that Microsoft is making about as much as OpenAI is selling access to their services."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "Chief Valley Cheerleader Casey Newton wrote on Platformer last week that diminishing returns in training models \"may not matter as much as you would guess,\" with his evidence being that Anthropic, who he claims \"has not been prone to hyperbole,\" do not think that scaling laws are ending."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "And even then, at some point somebody has to ask the question: why do we need all these GPUs if we've reached peak AI?"}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "The tech industry is over-leveraged, having doubled, tripled, quadrupled down on generative AI — a technology that doesn't do much more than it did a few months ago and won't do much more than it can do now."}, {"date": "2024-12-03", "title": "Godot Isn't Making it", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/godot-isnt-making-it", "quote": "If we're truly at the diminishing returns stage of transformer-based models, it will be extremely difficult to justify buying further iterations of NVIDIA GPUs past Blackwell."}, {"date": "2025-01-29", "title": "Deep Impact", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/deep-impact", "quote": "As I’ve said before, I believe we’re at peak AI, and now that generative AI has been commoditized, the only thing that OpenAI and Anthropic have left is their ability to innovate, which I’m not sure they’re capable of doing."}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "Large Language Models — which are trained by feeding them massive amounts of training data and then reinforcing their understanding through further training runs — are hitting the point of diminishing returns."}, {"date": "2025-04-14", "title": "OpenAI Is A Systemic Risk To The Tech Industry", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/openai-is-a-systemic-risk-to-the-tech-industry-2", "quote": "Worse still, investors and the media have run cover for the fact that these models don't really do much more than they did a year ago and for the overall diminishing returns of Large Language Models."}, {"date": "2025-05-27", "title": "Desperate Times, Desperate Measures", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/measures", "quote": "It has no moat, its models are hitting the point of diminishing returns and have been for some time, and as popular as ChatGPT may be, it isn't a business and constantly loses money. On top of that, it requires more money than has ever been invested in a startup."}, {"date": "2025-08-25", "title": "How To Argue With An AI Booster", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/how-to-argue-with-an-ai-booster", "quote": "Why Did This Happen? Because model developers hit a wall of diminishing returns, and the only way to make their models do more was to make them burn more tokens to generate a more accurate response (this is a very simple way of describing reasoning, a thing that OpenAI launched in September 2024 and others followed)."}], "verdict": "Mostly wrong", "analysis": "His 2024 <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_hit_wall__c2\" data-tip=\"cat_hit_wall__c2\" href=\"https://www.theargumentmag.com/p/ais-biggest-critic-has-lost-the-plot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">'Peak AI' and 'doesn't do much more than a year ago' calls</a> aged badly. <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_hit_wall__c4\" data-tip=\"cat_hit_wall__c4\" href=\"https://www.jonvet.com/blog/llm-scaling-in-2025\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Pre-training returns did flatten, a real and defensible point</a>, but <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_hit_wall__c3\" data-tip=\"cat_hit_wall__c3\" href=\"https://metr.org/blog/2025-03-19-measuring-ai-ability-to-complete-long-tasks/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">capability kept climbing via reasoning and reinforcement learning</a>, and <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_hit_wall__c1\" data-tip=\"cat_hit_wall__c1\" href=\"https://epoch.ai/data-insights/llm-inference-price-trends\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">inference cost for a fixed capability fell roughly 10x to 100x per year</a>. 'Pre-training is hitting diminishing returns' is fair. 'It has stopped improving' is not.", "srcs": [["LLM inference prices have fallen rapidly (Epoch AI)", "https://epoch.ai/data-insights/llm-inference-price-trends"], ["AI's biggest critic has lost the plot (Kelsey Piper, The Argument)", "https://www.theargumentmag.com/p/ais-biggest-critic-has-lost-the-plot"], ["Measuring AI ability to complete long tasks (METR, 2025)", "https://metr.org/blog/2025-03-19-measuring-ai-ability-to-complete-long-tasks/"]]}, {"id": "circular", "label": "Circular financing / Ponzi-like", "stakes": "S5", "scope": "industry-economics", "count": 13, "instances": [{"date": "2024-02-19", "title": "Subprime Intelligence", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sam-altman-fried", "quote": "Shell Games I believe we're reaching the upper limits about what generative AI can do and how accurate its outputs can be, and I believe that once reality catches up with artificial intelligence's marketing, there will be a dramatic knock-on effect that savages the entire tech industry."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "In any case, how do these neoclouds pay for their debt if the hyperscalers give up, or NVIDIA doesn’t send them money, or, more likely, private credit begins to notice that there’s no real revenue growth outside of circular compute deals with neoclouds’ largest supplier, investor and customer?"}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "Here’s A Diagram Of How Unbelievably Circular All The Money In AI Compute Has Become Credit to Anthony Restaino for this horrifying graphic:"}, {"date": "2025-12-08", "title": "NVIDIA Isn't Enron - So What Is It?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it", "quote": "It has plenty of money, and the circular deals it does with CoreWeave and Lambda don’t involve the same levels of risk."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "Davidson and Wagner at Aptus Capital — all raised circular deal concerns, but they were the minority, and those concerns were still often buried under buoyant optimism about the prospects of the company."}, {"date": "2026-03-03", "title": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-bubble-is-an-information-war", "quote": "## OpenAI’s Not-A-Ponzi-Scheme Revenues Talking of things that nobody seems to mind, on Friday Sam Altman accidentally said the quiet part out loud, live on CNBC, when asked about the very obviously circular deals with NVIDIA, Amazon and Microsoft (emphasis mine): Hey Sam, what does “the whole thing” refer to here?"}, {"date": "2026-03-03", "title": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-bubble-is-an-information-war", "quote": "Because I know you probably mean the AI industry, but this sounds exactly like a ponzi scheme! Now, jokes aside, ponzi schemes work entirely through feeding investor money to other investors."}, {"date": "2026-03-03", "title": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-bubble-is-an-information-war", "quote": "OpenAI and AI companies are not a ponzi scheme."}, {"date": "2026-03-03", "title": "The AI Bubble Is An Information War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-bubble-is-an-information-war", "quote": "Much like NVIDIA isn’t Enron, OpenAI isn’t a ponzi scheme."}, {"date": "2026-05-06", "title": "Am I Meant To Be Impressed?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/am-i-meant-to-be-impressed", "quote": "## Google Is Doing Circular Financing With Anthropic and Its TPUs, Selling TPUs To Anthropic, Who Then Pays To Rent Them Back From Google Yet things get weirder when you listen to Google’s most-recent earnings call: Interesting."}, {"date": "2026-05-06", "title": "Am I Meant To Be Impressed?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/am-i-meant-to-be-impressed", "quote": "Nevertheless, this entire industry is only made possible by the kayfabe circular economy of taking every single sign as good for AI and ignoring every possible glaring warning sign in the hopes that they’ll go away."}, {"date": "2026-05-12", "title": "Where Are All The Data Centers?", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/where-are-all-the-data-centers", "quote": "My last piece was a detailed commentary on the circular nature of the AI economy — and how the illusion of AI demand is just that, an illusion."}, {"date": "2026-05-26", "title": "Revenge of The Business Idiot", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-revenge-of-the-business-idiot", "quote": "Every single buy and sell-side analyst should have said CoreWeave, IREN, and other NVIDIA-backed neoclouds are dangerous investments fueled by circular finance."}], "verdict": "Genuinely mixed", "analysis": "More legitimate than 'just normal capitalism,' less than fraud. <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_circular__c1\" data-tip=\"cat_circular__c1\" href=\"https://www.theregister.com/2025/11/04/the_circular_economy_of_ai/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cross-entity vendor financing (NVIDIA into OpenAI, CoreWeave, Oracle)</a> can flatter separate companies' reported demand in a way intra-firm cross-subsidy cannot, and <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_circular__c2\" data-tip=\"cat_circular__c2\" href=\"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/11/11/big-short-investor-michael-burry-accuses-ai-hyperscalers-of-artificially-boosting-earnings.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mainstream analysts share the demand-durability and contagion worry</a>. But there is <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_circular__c3\" data-tip=\"cat_circular__c3\" href=\"https://www.venturesedge.io/articles/ai-roundtripping-nvidia-openai-oracle-and-the-circular-financing-debate\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">real economic substance, chips ship and data centers get built</a>, <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_circular__c4\" data-tip=\"cat_circular__c4\" href=\"https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NVIDIA is cash-rich and clean-audited</a>, and <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_circular__c5\" data-tip=\"cat_circular__c5\" href=\"https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">he himself concedes 'NVIDIA Isn't Enron.'</a>", "srcs": [["NVIDIA Isn't Enron, So What Is It? (Zitron, Dec 2025)", "https://www.wheresyoured.at/nvidia-isnt-enron-so-what-is-it"], ["Burry accuses AI hyperscalers of boosting earnings (CNBC, Nov 2025)", "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/11/11/big-short-investor-michael-burry-accuses-ai-hyperscalers-of-artificially-boosting-earnings.html"]]}, {"id": "no_demand", "label": "Nobody wants it / no real demand", "stakes": "S2", "scope": "demand-adoption", "count": 11, "instances": [{"date": "2024-05-13", "title": "Expectations Versus Reality", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/expectations-versus-reality", "quote": "Nobody needs this crap!"}, {"date": "2025-02-24", "title": "There Is No AI Revolution", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/wheres-the-money", "quote": "This software is being forced on people at scale by corporations desperate to seem futuristic without any real understanding as to why they need it, and whatever use cases may exist for Large Language Models are dwarfed by how utterly unprofitable this whole fiasco is."}, {"date": "2025-03-03", "title": "Power Cut", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/power-cut", "quote": "It is as if nobody wants to think about this too hard — that nobody wants to stop the party, to accept what’s been staring us in the face since last year, and when given the most egregious, glaring evidence they must find ways to dismiss it rather than give it the energy it deserves."}, {"date": "2025-03-24", "title": "The Phony Comforts of AI Optimism", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/optimistic-cowardice", "quote": "My core theses — The Rot Economy (that the tech industry has become dominated by growth), The Rot-Com Bubble (that the tech industry has run out of hyper-growth ideas), and that generative AI has created a kind of capitalist death cult where nobody wants to admit that they're not making any money — are far from comfortable."}, {"date": "2025-06-16", "title": "Sincerity Wins The War", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/sic", "quote": "Nobody wants to be destitute."}, {"date": "2025-06-30", "title": "Make Fun Of Them", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/make-fun-of-them", "quote": "Put aside however you feel about generative AI for a second and face one very simple point: it doesn’t do enough, it’s really not cool at all, and we’re being forced to use it."}, {"date": "2025-07-21", "title": "The Hater's Guide To The AI Bubble", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-haters-gui", "quote": "We are being forced to use it by bosses, or services we like that now insist it's part of our documents or our search engines, not because it does something, but because those pushing it need us to use it to prove that they know what's going on."}, {"date": "2025-09-29", "title": "The Case Against Generative AI", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-case-against-generative-ai", "quote": "I am telling you, as I have been telling you for years, again and again and again, that the demand is not there for generative AI, and the demand is never, ever arriving. The only reason anyone humours any of this crap is the endless hoarding of GPUs to build capacity for a revolution that will never arrive."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "OpenAI and Anthropic are going to be even worse. This is why nobody wants to take AI companies public."}, {"date": "2025-12-29", "title": "The Enshittifinancial Crisis", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-enshittifinancial-crisis", "quote": "This is why nobody wants to talk about the actual costs of AI."}, {"date": "2026-03-24", "title": "The AI Industry Is Lying To You", "url": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/the-ai-industry-is-lying-to-you", "quote": "The smug, condescending army of AI boosters exists to make you look away from the harsh truth — AI makes very little revenue, lacks tangible productivity benefits, and seems to, at scale, actively harm the productivity and efficacy of the workers that are being forced to use it."}], "verdict": "Mostly wrong, refuted by his own reporting", "analysis": "'Nobody wants it, it was forced on everyone' is contradicted by <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_no_demand__c1\" data-tip=\"cat_no_demand__c1\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/02/27/chatgpt-reaches-900m-weekly-active-users/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">about 900M weekly users</a> and <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_no_demand__c2\" data-tip=\"cat_no_demand__c2\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/02/27/chatgpt-reaches-900m-weekly-active-users/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">tens of millions of paying subscribers</a>. The sharpest rebuttal is internal. His own scoops on enormous Claude Code and Codex spend are direct evidence of the demand he denies, because <a class=\"cite\" data-c=\"cat_no_demand__c4\" data-tip=\"cat_no_demand__c4\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/sectors/technology/articles/company-blew-500m-claude-ai-173519468.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">companies do not accidentally burn hundreds of millions on tools nobody uses</a>. His more defensible point is about willingness-to-pay at a profitable price, not the absence of demand.", "srcs": [["ChatGPT statistics: ~900M weekly users, ~25B ARR (2026)", "https://technologychecker.io/blog/chatgpt-statistics"], ["AI's biggest critic has lost the plot (Kelsey Piper, The Argument)", "https://www.theargumentmag.com/p/ais-biggest-critic-has-lost-the-plot"]]}]